": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 703186, "labels": ["Desire Hotfix", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-01T16:13:08Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-14T14:52:23Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1489", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1612", "record": {"id": "ENG-1612", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_8140f09bf9f1b94c", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1612", "number": 1612, "title": "The tutorial text issues and missing translations icons for milestone previews", "description": "* The level 1 tutorial texts are the old ones.\n\n  [RPReplay_Final1727859941.MP4]([URL_51304])\n* Level 5 +3 boost tutorial has missing translations for both texts.\n\n  ![image.png]([URL_51303])\n* Level 6 level objective tutorial has the old text\n\n  ![image.png]([URL_51302])\n* The rectangle overlap still visible in jumbo tile tutorial level \n\n  ![image.png]([URL_51301])\n* Missing translation on lucky drop milestone & its icon should be added\n\n  ![image.png]([URL_51300])\n* We still unlock every minigame at ch2 lvl6\n* Vanishing tile milestone icon isn't up-to date.\n* Quest milestone has the old icon.\n\n  ![image.png]([URL_51299])\n  1. quests are unlocked at level 15 without any tutorial\n\n     [RPReplay_Final1727861919.MP4]([URL_51298])\n  2. then after level 16 it's tutorial started.\n\n     [RPReplay_Final1727862006.MP4]([URL_51297])\n* River tile has missing translation.\n\n  ![image.png]([URL_51296])", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2024-10-04T10:07:35Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-04-10T07:35:19Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 716247, "labels": ["Desire Release", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2024-10-02T14:20:08Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-09T15:13:08Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1491", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1614", "record": {"id": "ENG-1614", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1385", "assignee_id": "usr_caafeec2804b3a67", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1614", "number": 1614, "title": "The Win & Collect Event Pop up UI & VFX Issues", "description": "The new event pop up has some new ui and VFX issues. \n\n* There is no indication that there is an event. It can only be understood after getting the first event token. \n  * The expected outcome to auto trigger the event pop up when it's unlocked. \n* The slider on top the button is not reflect the actual progression. (It's 25% filled with 0 tokens)\n\n  [RPReplay_Final1727867052.MP4]([URL_51320])\n* The level quit confirmatory pop up has undimmed pixels on the edges. (The earlier version doesn't have that issue)\n\n  ![image.png]([URL_51319])\n  * The confirmatory pop up should not spawn or the text should be updated because it spawns every time. \n\n    ![image.png]([URL_51318])\n\n  ![image.png]([URL_51317])\n* The confirmatory pop up is not spawned when the quit screen is triggered by the out of moves screen. \n\n  [Screen_Recording_20241009_174720_Domino Delights.mp4]([URL_51316])\n* Character is lost, when player tries to resume after the confirmatory pop up. \n\n  [Screen_Recording_20241009_175618_Domino Delights.mp4]([URL_51315])\n* It gives 3 butterfly regardless of event tokens earned\n\n  [RPReplay_Final1727867052.MP4]([URL_51314])\n  * Even quitting the level triggers the event token VFXs.\n  * Even with chapter changes, it's triggered every in every saga map scene awake.\n\n    [RPReplay_Final1727879704.MP4]([URL_51313])\n* The event button is above everything and every screen.\n\n  [RPReplay_Final1727871493.MP4]([URL_51312])\n* The token animation is a little bit off because the slider disappears before all butterflies arrives.\n* The event duration is static 0m 0 s\n\n  ![image.png]([URL_51311])\n* The butterfly icon is not centered.\n\n  ![image.png]([URL_51310])\n* Magical Wings Modal also has incomplete dimmed background showing lit background on top and bottom of the phone screen\n* The duration is 0m 0s on the pop up.\n* The reward sprite is not updated by the progress.\n  * It should show the item sprite if it gives 1 reward.\n  * If more than one, we should show the chest and show the rewards on tooltip of chest. \n\n    ![image.png]([URL_51309])\n* Magical Wings Event description could use some grammar and punctuation clean up. ask @[PERSON_NAME_0054] for better explanation. \n* The first two rewards are not obvious.\n\n  ![image.png]([URL_51308])\n  * The rewards after those have all reward sprites even though most of them aren't rewarded. \n    * The reward screen is always the same for all rewards.\n\n      ![image.png]([URL_51307])\n* If player earns more token than the milestone cap, the progress bar show 4/3 and the 1 surplus token isn't added to the next milestone. \n  * It should show 3/3 and complete the vfx for that particular milestone.\n    * Then it should show that the later milestone is filled by 1 token. \n\n      [Screen_Recording_20241009_171433_Domino Delights_1.mp4]([URL_51306])\n* The token VFX glows bleed through other screens like quests\n\n  [RPReplay_Final1728472437.MP4]([URL_51305])", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-07T15:52:57Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-17T17:06:35Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 697108, "labels": ["Lava Hot Fix"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-1623", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-02T14:43:41Z", "updated_at": "2024-11-12T13:51:03Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1495", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1618", "record": {"id": "ENG-1618", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_caafeec2804b3a67", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1618", "number": 1618, "title": "Music & SFX Toggleability Issues", "description": "[[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5824].0267711.mp4]([URL_51326])\n\n* [We have missing click sounds.](https://linear.app/harmonygames-games/issue/ENG-1563/clicking-sound-missing-from-a-lot-of-button-clicks)\n* **Active SFXs with Disabled SFX button on main game**\n  * The matching action SFX scale\n  * The gold tile boost sound\n  * Coin SFX from streak rewards\n  * Character token sound\n  * The +1 & +2 tile streak ability VFX (ability VFXs in general)\n  * Streak announcer\n  * Win sound\n  * Tile conversion to token sound\n* **In river tile,**\n  * the SFX and music preferences is not visually saved but functionally saved.\n  * Game music comes with toggling the music button\n  * However, the SFXs are not by toggling them\n* **In memory tile,**\n  * SFXs are controlled by the music button.\n* **In tile dozer,**\n  * Both music and SFXs are tied to the SFX button.\n* **In lucky drop,**\n  * SFXs are enabled in every cases that it's not related to the buttons on home.\n* **Independent sounds from both buttons:**\n  * The tile conversion sound in the core game enabled even though music and SFX are disabled.", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-17T21:16:35Z", "completed_at": "2025-01-16T18:05:08Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 566009, "labels": ["Easy Fix - Just do it!", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-1563", "type": "relates"}, {"target": "ENG-1894", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-02T15:38:42Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-16T18:05:08Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1502", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1624", "record": {"id": "ENG-1624", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_Robert", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1624", "number": 1624, "title": "When +3 Tile and +2 Gold Tile boosts are BOTH active, wrong amount of tiles given at start", "description": "When both boost are active, instead of 3 regular tiles and 2 gold tiles added at start, the player is given 1 regular tile short. So instead of 3 + 2 it became only 2 + 2. When power-ups are independently active, they work just fine.\n\n# ~~UPDATED INFO~~ \n\n~~I don't think that's the issue, I feel like the +3 time boost is just changed or broken because I got only +3 from the river tile but in the core game, I got 2 wild tiles as well. So we might use +3 as 2 wild tiles and 2-wild tile as a null.~~\n\n[RPReplay_Final1727961630.MOV]([URL_51330])", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-07T16:55:46Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-18T17:25:47Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 695649, "labels": ["Lava Hot Fix", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-02T21:00:58Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-18T17:25:47Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1503", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1625", "record": {"id": "ENG-1625", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_EMPLOYEE_0032", "creator_id": "usr_Robert", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1625", "number": 1625, "title": "Mini Game Token Balance Management", "description": "'@[PERSON_NAME_0054] said:\n\n> 1. By default, without upgrades from Lexi, the max cap of tokens a player can store is 50. HOWEVER\n> 2. If during a live game in Lucky Drop or Dozer, players was able to earn beyond the cap, they are allowed to do so. For example if I pushed 5000 tokens down the prize pit in Dozer, I will have a balance of 5000. This stays at 5000 even if I were to leave the game, play a main game, come back. 5000. If I go play lucky drop, 5000. I take a break, go on the toilet, come back, 5000.\n> 3. When the balance exceeds the cap, all regeneration activity stops.\n> 4. When either dozer or luckydrop is LIVE (meaning actively played by a player), the regeneration if 1 token per 3 minutes. When the player is offline, it is also currently 3 minutes, however these 2 variables might change in the future so please make sure your code supports that.\n> 5. The balance is shared between both dozer and lucky drop\n> 6. The UI is suppose to work like this:\n>     a. Timer counts from 3 minute down to 0.\n>     b. When timer is at 3 minutes, bar = empty\n>     c. When timer is at 0 seconds, bar = 100% full.\n>     d. This let's the players know bar filled = new token, and at the same time they know how much time is left before the bar is filled.\n> 7. Players can earn tokens from the main game from excessive left over hand tiles. THESE TILES CANNOT EXCEED THE CAP OF 50. (Or the upgraded max cap)\n> 8. A red notification icon will be shown over the mini game button on the home screen bottom UI", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-03T12:43:50Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-08T14:26:11Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 710228, "labels": ["Desire Hotfix"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-02T21:17:34Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-08T14:26:11Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1510", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1631", "record": {"id": "ENG-1631", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1631", "number": 1631, "title": "The rewind cost is not centered", "description": "On both platforms, the alignment issue of the rewind price is back. It\u2019s left-aligned rather than middle-aligned\n\n![image.png]([URL_51333])", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-07T15:22:00Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-10T16:00:44Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 707254, "labels": ["Easy Fix - Just do it!", "Desire Hotfix", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-1427", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-03T12:38:55Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-10T16:00:44Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1512", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1633", "record": {"id": "ENG-1633", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1351", "assignee_id": "usr_caafeec2804b3a67", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1633", "number": 1633, "title": "Tooltips text alignment looks weird", "description": "The bottom part of the speech bubble has less area than the upper part, meaning that the text is not centered both vertically and horizontally. \n\n![image.png]([URL_51337])\n\n![image.png]([URL_51336])\n\n![image.png]([URL_51335])\n\n![image.png]([URL_51334])", "priority": 4, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-08T15:43:30Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-10T16:18:03Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 707236, "labels": ["Easy Fix - Just do it!", "Desire Hotfix"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-03T13:58:09Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-10T16:18:03Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1518", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1639", "record": {"id": "ENG-1639", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1639", "number": 1639, "title": "Unmatchable tiles at levels with both bomb and mega tiles", "description": "Mega and bomb tiles didn't change their icon to fire. \n\nThe regular tile changed the acorn to the fire but the acorn is visible for both advanced tiles. \n\nHowever, the bomb tile symbol is stated as fire functionally while mega tile symbol is just acorn. So that might create the discrepancy on visually matching but not functional scenarios. \n\nChapter 2 Level 10\n\n![image.png]([URL_51348])\n\n[[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5826].5739884.mp4]([URL_51347])\n\n![image.png]([URL_51346])\n\n![image.png]([URL_51345])\n\n[RPReplay_Final1728049483.MP4]([URL_51344])\n\n[Screen Recording [CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5825].mp4]([URL_51343])", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-07T23:02:07Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-08T14:22:02Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 710232, "labels": ["Desire Hotfix", "Bug", "UA Blocker"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-1601", "type": "relates"}, {"target": "ENG-1634", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-04T14:48:21Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-09T03:28:48Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1552", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1671", "record": {"id": "ENG-1671", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_Robert", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1671", "number": 1671, "title": "Jumbo tile spawns a bunch of repeat tiles", "description": "I get 2/2/1/1 type tiles very often\n\nI also get 2/2/2/1 type tiles quite often\n\nI have even seen 2/2/2/2 tiles.\n\nWe need to make sure the sequencer is pulling from the right pool or randomizing correctly. Right now it doesn't seem like it's randomizing 2 out of the 4 symbols as originally intended (The first 2 symbols being part of the sequence)", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-11-04T18:52:20Z", "completed_at": "2024-11-05T12:12:18Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 670042, "labels": ["Puzzle Engine", "Destiny"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-08T17:42:19Z", "updated_at": "2024-11-05T12:12:18Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1554", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1673", "record": {"id": "ENG-1673", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_8140f09bf9f1b94c", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1673", "number": 1673, "title": "Consider Tutorial Completed If Level Won", "description": "If a tutorial starts with a \"puzzle started\" trigger or level requirement trigger, the tutorial system should consider it complete if the level is won. This is for edge cases in which a player wins the level without completing the tutorial requirement, and subsequently, the tutorial order gets broken.", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-12-09T17:42:49Z", "completed_at": "2025-01-16T18:07:30Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 566007, "labels": ["Tutorial Editor"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-09T13:48:55Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-16T18:07:30Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1575", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1692", "record": {"id": "ENG-1692", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_63fffeb4fab5233e", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1692", "number": 1692, "title": "Add tooltips for 'leauges' and 'leadersboards' buttons", "description": "'@Leonard said:\n\n> Minor to-do but both \u201cleauges\u201d and \u201cleadersboards\u201d lost their tooltip. When you click on them - they should say \u201ccoming soon\u201d @[PERSON_NAME_0054]. Can anyone tackle this? I don\u2019t have a ticket yet\n\n![IMG_8429.PNG]([URL_51394])", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-28T15:25:52Z", "completed_at": "2024-11-18T17:53:02Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 650981, "labels": ["Easy Fix - Just do it!", "Sprint 25 Destiny - Nov 8th", "Destiny"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-09T23:37:31Z", "updated_at": "2024-11-18T17:53:02Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1583", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-17", "record": {"id": "ENG-17", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-16", "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-17", "number": 17, "title": "Character Select/Profile Screens", "description": "Only way to select or change character is through the \"pre-level\" dialog and through the character button on bottom navigation bar.\n\nDuring game play the selected character will be displayed on bottom left of screen.\n\nDuring home screen, the last used character will be displayed as avatar icon.\n\nBehavior of the selection + profile screen is seen here:\n\n![image.png]([URL_13513])\n\nLink to Figma: [[URL_13512])", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": "2023-11-10", "started_at": "2023-08-07T19:06:18Z", "completed_at": "2024-01-03T06:22:04Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 1115160, "labels": ["Characters", "Sprint 7 - November 10th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2023-03-22T19:38:21Z", "updated_at": "2024-01-03T06:22:04Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1589", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1704", "record": {"id": "ENG-1704", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1511", "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_Robert", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1704", "number": 1704, "title": "Update Nate and Julius tile removal hidden bias to 100% + 2 new rules removing vanishing tile. Update Lexi as well", "description": "The rule originally only trigger 40% of the time, let's make that 100%. We also inserted 2 new rules so it can now remove vanishing tile\n\n 1. (NEW) A vanishing face up tile that does not connect with any tile ON THE BOARD AND TILE IN HAND.\n 2. A face up tile that does not connect with any tile ON THE BOARD AND TILE IN HAND.\n 3. A face up tile that does not connect with any tile ON THE BOARD ONLY\n 4. A face up tile that does not connect with any TILE IN HAND\n 5. A face up tile that's a twin tile, AKA transitory tile (Both side = same symbol)\n 6. (NEW) Any vanishing tile\n 7. A face up tile that has only 1 of 2 symbols that connects with ANY TILE ON BOARD AND TILE IN HAND\n 8. A face up tile that has only 1 of 2 symbols that connects with ANY TILE ON BOARD\n 9. A face up tile that has only 1 of 2 symbols that connects with TILE IN HAND\n10. Finally, if none of the tiles satisfy any of the criteria above, random tile is removed.\n\nAt higher level Julius will remove 2 of these tiles. The target check is independent for each removal. So he can remove 2 bad piece, 2 good pieces, or 1 of each as a result.\n\nLexi's targeting of key tiles, increase probability of 35% -> 50% please.\n\nPlease also have her prioritize fire symbols for levels with fire tiles.", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-22T15:47:12Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-25T15:44:10Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 685670, "labels": ["Spells/Abilities", "Improvement", "Destiny"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-11T22:31:27Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-25T15:44:10Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1595", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-171", "record": {"id": "ENG-171", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "EPI-9", "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_Robert", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-171", "number": 171, "title": "Puzzle Layout Editor Mass Improvements", "description": "Three epic quality of life puzzle editor improvements, see sub-issues for details:\n\n1) Auto snap grid/offset system for overlapping tiles\n\n2) Rotational increments for tile while holding down a button while rotating\n\n3) Auto align with other tiles on layout\n\nThese features should have the ability to be enabled via a checkbox for on/off.", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2023-09-28T19:39:30Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 1251355, "labels": ["Puzzle Editor", "Main Game"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2023-09-02T20:12:33Z", "updated_at": "2023-09-28T19:39:30Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1601", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1715", "record": {"id": "ENG-1715", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1543", "assignee_id": "usr_bdf01b53c6a92c5e", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1715", "number": 1715, "title": "The lucky drop reward screen UI issues", "description": "Version or date: ios 0.2.206\n\n### Description: \n\n* The no prize earned screen is not implemented. Instead, it still shows the empty reward screen.\n* The amount of tokens earned is still visible which should be removed from the list of reward items because it's confusing for players. \n* The text of individual reward amounts are too close each other. The digits are sort of overlapping. \n\n### Visual References:\n\n[RPReplay_Final1729848502.MP4]([URL_51423])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to reflect the changes in the UI part. \n\n![image.png]([URL_51422])\n\n---\n\n---\n\nCurrently the out of token flow is implemented, yet the no reward flow is not implemented. \n\n![Screenshot_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5845]-67_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.jpg]([URL_51421])\n\nThe implementation should be like the screenshot below. See the parent ticket for the figma link. [ENG-1543](https://linear.app/harmonygames-games/issue/ENG-1543/implement-additional-reward-screen-for-both-mini-games-when-no-prizes)", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-28T15:47:42Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-31T19:53:21Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 676781, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-1719", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-15T14:33:14Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-31T19:53:21Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1605", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1719", "record": {"id": "ENG-1719", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1697", "assignee_id": "usr_EMPLOYEE_0032", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1719", "number": 1719, "title": "Remove the tile token amount from the win screen of both lucky drop and tile dozer", "description": null, "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-18T16:12:30Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-21T15:52:42Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-04-26T07:35:46Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 691422, "labels": [], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-1715", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2024-10-15T17:22:37Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-25T14:13:38Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1606", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-172", "record": {"id": "ENG-172", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-171", "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_Robert", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-172", "number": 172, "title": "Auto snap grid/offset system for overlapping tiles", "description": "A system that basically does this:\n\n![image.png]([URL_13540])\n\nMost likely done by offsets of geographical center of one domino piece to another, in 25% increments (maybe we should allow user to specify? (I.E 10%, 20%, 25%, 33.3%, 50% and other multiples of 100)\n\n![image.png]([URL_13539])\n\nThe idea is that the pieces will automatically snap into these grid positions over another tile, if the feature is checked on in the checkbox.", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2023-09-21T12:06:33Z", "completed_at": "2023-09-28T19:39:18Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 1251355, "labels": ["Puzzle Editor", "Sprint 4 - September 29th", "Main Game"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2023-09-02T20:13:12Z", "updated_at": "2023-09-28T19:39:18Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1616", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-173", "record": {"id": "ENG-173", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-171", "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_Robert", "state_id": "Canceled", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-173", "number": 173, "title": "Rotational increments for tile while holding down a button while rotating", "description": "We want to be able to rotate pieces in 15 degree increments accurately, like this, the video is 45 degree increments, but we want 15 in ours. You hold down shift button to trigger toggle the auto increments.\n\n[Rotational Increments.mp4]([URL_13542])\n\n![image.png]([URL_13541])", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": "2023-09-19T17:31:40Z", "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 1264443, "labels": ["Puzzle Editor", "Sprint 4 - September 29th", "Main Game"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2023-09-02T20:13:28Z", "updated_at": "2023-09-19T17:31:40Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1620", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-174", "record": {"id": "ENG-174", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-171", "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_Robert", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-174", "number": 174, "title": "Auto align with other tiles on layout", "description": "Basically snap to align with other tiles nearby:\n\n![image.png]([URL_13544])\n\n[Auto Alignment.mp4]([URL_13543])", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2023-09-20T00:42:53Z", "completed_at": "2023-09-28T19:39:15Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 1251355, "labels": ["Puzzle Editor", "Sprint 4 - September 29th", "Main Game"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2023-09-02T20:13:34Z", "updated_at": "2023-09-28T19:39:15Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1624", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1743", "record": {"id": "ENG-1743", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_PERSON_3233", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1743", "number": 1743, "title": "Character screen button and character buttons are broken.", "description": "The character selection screen is buggy. There are couple of issues:\n\n1. If the character button is clicked\n   1. clicking on other navigation buttons (except the home button) is not directing to the clicked sections. \n   2. clicking on minigame button changes the top HUD to the minigame hub top HUD. \n2. If any other navigation button is clicked, clicking character button is not directing to the character screen.\n   1. if minigame button is clicked, clicking on the char button is disabling the top HUD.\n3. In the char screen via the button, the first click on characters disables the bottom HUD.\n   1. The 2nd click directs to the selected character. \n4. The close button in character screens are not working in the first click, but works on the 2nd click. \n5. The first click on the characters in the prelevel dialogue is not directing to the selected character page. \n\n[Record_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5852]_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.mp4]([URL_51461])\n\n[Record_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5851]_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.mp4]([URL_51460])", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-21T16:18:28Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-24T15:32:31Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 687122, "labels": ["Lava Hot Fix", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-21T15:43:48Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-24T15:32:31Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1627", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1746", "record": {"id": "ENG-1746", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1746", "number": 1746, "title": "The chapter completion tutorial is broken by fast click", "description": "All tutorials happen outside of the board scene have those kind of edge cases where clicking another place is possible before the tutorials are triggered because the input blocking is also triggered by the tutorial's presence. \n\nIn that case, there is a small gap where players can click on anywhere they want and creates a FTUE blocker, leading to non-functional highlighted areas.  \n\n[Screen Recording [CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5854].mp4]([URL_51465])\n\nSteps to Repro:\n\n1. Complete level 15.\n2. Start spamming character or shop buttons\n3. Observe that the chapter button is highlighted on a different screen. \n\n## Version or date:\n\n## Description:\n\n## Visual References:\n\n[RPReplay_Final1729846606.MP4]([URL_51464])\n\n## Expected Outcome:\n\n## Steps to Repro:\n\n##", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-24T12:30:37Z", "completed_at": "2024-11-04T11:38:58Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 671515, "labels": ["Tutorial Editor", "Lava Hot Fix", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-21T15:59:13Z", "updated_at": "2024-11-04T11:38:58Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1628", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1747", "record": {"id": "ENG-1747", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_8140f09bf9f1b94c", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1747", "number": 1747, "title": "Tutorial highlights don't scale properly for tablets", "description": "2 issues regarding highlights in general \n\n1. During Leonardo we added the ability to play with highlight scales but they don't really work \n2. We got reports that highlights on tablets look too small (aka they don't rescale properly for different resolutions)", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-24T00:57:09Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-31T21:04:03Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 676710, "labels": ["Tutorial Editor"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-21T16:14:36Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-31T21:04:03Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1633", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1751", "record": {"id": "ENG-1751", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_caafeec2804b3a67", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1751", "number": 1751, "title": "Buzzing Sound and FPS drop in level ends.", "description": "There is an error on both android and ios in the early levels that causes FPS drop and buzzing sound. It start where the coins are about to float to the balance and when level completed text is visible.  \n\n[Record_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5856]_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.mp4]([URL_51471])\n\n[RPReplay_Final1729603602.MP4]([URL_51470])\n\n![Screenshot_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5855]-73_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.jpg]([URL_51469])\n\n![image.png]([URL_51468])\n\n`ArgumentNullException: Value cannot be null. Parameter name: source UnityEngine.AudioSource.PlayOneShot (UnityEngine.AudioClip clip, System.Single volumeScale) (at <7ff808ccd2ab4663b6bfd6771e926301>:0) SagaMapAudio.PlayCollectCoinSound () (at Assets/GoD/Scripts/SagaMap/SagaMapAudio.cs:80) LevelCompletePopupController.PlayCoinSound () (at Assets/GoD/Scripts/UI/Popups/LevelCompletePopupController.cs:61) LevelCompletePopupController+<PlayCoinSounds>d__9.MoveNext () (at Assets/GoD/Scripts/UI/Popups/LevelCompletePopupController.cs:72) UnityEngine.SetupCoroutine.InvokeMoveNext (System.Collections.IEnumerator enumerator, System.IntPtr returnValueAddress) (at <0b78209fd00d4f419f30dd210cbab239>:0) UnityEngine.DebugLogHandler:LogException(Exception, Object) HarmonyLogging.HarmonyLoggingFilter:LogException(Exception, Object) (at Assets/GoD/Scripts/Utils/Logging/HarmonyLog.cs:86) HarmonyLogging.HarmonyLoggingFilter:LogException(Exception, Object) (at Assets/GoD/Scripts/Utils/Logging/HarmonyLog.cs:86) HarmonyLogging.HarmonyLoggingFilter:LogException(Exception, Object) (at Assets/GoD/Scripts/Utils/Logging/HarmonyLog.cs:86) UnityEngine.Debug:CallOverridenDebugHandler(Exception, Object)`", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-22T21:07:52Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-23T13:51:47Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 688662, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-22T16:44:50Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-23T13:51:47Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1635", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1753", "record": {"id": "ENG-1753", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1753", "number": 1753, "title": "Quest tutorial is broken with pop up offers and fast click", "description": "When player gets new offers just after finishing the level 16 or after starting a new session, the quest tutorial is blocked by that. But clicking the quest button is not fixing the issue though. Because usually if the highlighted button is clickable, player can click and complete the tutorial. \n\n[Record_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5859]_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.mp4]([URL_51474])", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-23T21:26:16Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-25T12:34:16Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 685860, "labels": ["Tutorial Editor", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-1749", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-22T16:58:37Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-25T12:34:16Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1636", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1754", "record": {"id": "ENG-1754", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1754", "number": 1754, "title": "The time boost tutorial is broken by fast click", "description": "Clicking play button quickly creates an issue where the highlight is not gone. However, the tutorial should be terminated with that button click and hide every highlight. When I killed the app, the tutorial seems finished. \n\nThe highlight stays on the screen even though the tutorial can be marked as completed. \n\n[RPReplay_Final1729604566.MP4]([URL_51475])", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-23T21:25:46Z", "completed_at": "2024-10-25T16:26:48Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 685627, "labels": ["Tutorial Editor", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-22T17:01:12Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-25T16:26:48Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1645", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1762", "record": {"id": "ENG-1762", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Backlog", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1762", "number": 1762, "title": "Visiting shop after the out of moves doesn't retrigger the out of moves", "description": "If a player visits the in-level store after the out of moves screen, the out of moves can't be triggered by tap anywhere. But it also is triggered by clicking on both the hand and board tiles. \n\n[Screen_Recording_20241022_214957_Domino Delights.mp4]([URL_51487])\n\n[Screen_Recording_20241022_212153_Domino Delights.mp4]([URL_51486])", "priority": 4, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 590432, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-23T14:45:55Z", "updated_at": "2024-12-30T19:02:42Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1652", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1769", "record": {"id": "ENG-1769", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_63fffeb4fab5233e", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1769", "number": 1769, "title": "Mixup inliveops_completion event and wrong Mini-Game Event Properties", "description": "We don't have any data **on luckydrop and tiledozer** in **mini_game** event the **mini_game_summary** at all**.**\n\nIn version 0.2.40, there are 2 types of **mini_game** events showing different property profiles. One of the profiles we believe belongs to **quest** event.There are 3 mini_game events being received in 0.2.40, but since live ops is disabled on the live build, we should not be receiving any of these events.\n\n![image.png]([URL_51498])\n\nAdditionally, in **mini_game** event the **mini_game_summary** field doesn't follow the data dictionary. We are missing `reason` (we can postpone this) and `to` means tiles on the board when the level begins so it can't be zero but it should capture number of the available tiles when the level starts.\n\nWe are also sending empty strings, when empty please send \"0\" instead.\n\nFor instance memory game sends this\n\n\\[ir=0;nrm=2;rc=\\[li:1;co:40\\];iw=1;re=;ih=;di=easy;to=0;sa=\\[(3,2),(4,1),(5,1)\\]\\]\n\nIt should be this instead\n\n\\[ir=0;nrm=2;rc=\\[li:1;co:40\\];iw=1;re=0;ih=0;di=easy;to=24;sa=\\[(3,2),(4,1),(5,1)\\]\\]\n\nRiver Tile data is available", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-10-25T00:45:27Z", "completed_at": "2025-01-16T18:05:08Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-07-17T03:19:41Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 566009, "labels": ["Lava Hot Fix"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2024-10-24T21:58:22Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-16T18:05:08Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1658", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1774", "record": {"id": "ENG-1774", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_bdf01b53c6a92c5e", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1774", "number": 1774, "title": "Lucky Drop Slot Reward Issues", "description": "Version or date: ios 0.2.206\n\n### Description: \n\nThere are couple of Lucky Drop issues in terms of reward appeared on slots both functionally and visually. \n\nI almost spent 300 tokens on that game. What I've gotten from those sessions are like lots of coins (I mean mostly 1 coin), and tile tokens. Only different rewards I got are 1 gust and 10 stars. However as I checked the GDD, it should grant much more diverse reward than that.\n\n* It doesn't grant the guaranteed reward for certain threshold levels lie level 10 20 etc. \n* I didn't get any hero tokens nor gems despite having so high chance to get at least one because of the levels slot gets upgraded. \n\n### Visual References:\n\n[RPReplay_Final1729847750.MP4]([URL_51505])\n\n[RPReplay_Final1729857673.MP4]([URL_51504])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to sync the possibility of rewards with the GDD like giving the guaranteed reward and establishing reward possibilities of slots rather than just the most probable reward and jackpot reward. \n\n[[URL_51295])\n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Throw as much as token until getting high levels of slots. \n2. Observe its behavior when the level reaches to 60 70 80 etc\n3. Observe there is less reward than it's intended behavior.", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2024-10-28T14:53:41Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 681401, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-25T14:06:09Z", "updated_at": "2024-10-28T14:53:41Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1663", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1779", "record": {"id": "ENG-1779", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_8140f09bf9f1b94c", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1779", "number": 1779, "title": "Puzzle Editor Bot Next Steps", "description": "As discussed, here are the next steps to improve the puzzle editor bot.", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-05-05T19:16:05Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 408978, "labels": ["Bot"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-28T15:24:32Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T19:16:05Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1664", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-178", "record": {"id": "ENG-178", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-171", "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-178", "number": 178, "title": "Add hand tile count to puzzle settings", "description": null, "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2023-09-15T17:50:21Z", "completed_at": "2023-09-28T19:39:10Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 1251355, "labels": ["Puzzle Editor", "Sprint 4 - September 29th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2023-09-06T18:00:38Z", "updated_at": "2023-09-28T19:39:10Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1665", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1780", "record": {"id": "ENG-1780", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1779", "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_8140f09bf9f1b94c", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1780", "number": 1780, "title": "Bot can play vanishing tiles", "description": "In addition to its current logic, the bot should prioritize matching a vanishing tile where it can.", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-11-25T19:14:20Z", "completed_at": "2025-01-16T18:05:09Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 566009, "labels": [], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-28T15:24:32Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-16T18:05:09Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1666", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1781", "record": {"id": "ENG-1781", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1779", "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_8140f09bf9f1b94c", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1781", "number": 1781, "title": "Puzzle editor can play bomb tiles", "description": "In addition to its current logic, the bot can play bomb levels in the following way. \n\n1. It prioritizes a fire token where it can\n2. It prioritizes blowing a bomb if it's lit", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-11-25T19:15:06Z", "completed_at": "2025-01-16T18:05:09Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 566009, "labels": ["Levels", "Puzzle Editor"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-28T15:24:32Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-16T18:05:09Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1667", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1782", "record": {"id": "ENG-1782", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1779", "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_8140f09bf9f1b94c", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1782", "number": 1782, "title": "Match the bot with current data", "description": "We need to match our bot with the current data to figure out how accurately we can predict a win rate. I have two approaches for this: \n\n1. To compare simple win stats \n2. To match the \"moves\" event in metabase and report what players are doing differently than the bot. We can use the hardcoded level 2 as a pilot.", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-05-05T19:16:08Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 408978, "labels": ["Nova Release"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-28T15:24:32Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T19:16:08Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1669", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1784", "record": {"id": "ENG-1784", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1779", "assignee_id": "usr_bdf01b53c6a92c5e", "creator_id": "usr_8140f09bf9f1b94c", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1784", "number": 1784, "title": "Puzzle editor performance improvement", "description": "The puzzle editor is essentially a scene in the engine and therefore performs very poorly over extended use which we have to frequently.", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-05-05T19:16:08Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 408978, "labels": ["Puzzle Editor", "Improvement"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-28T15:25:37Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T19:16:08Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1670", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1785", "record": {"id": "ENG-1785", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1779", "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_8140f09bf9f1b94c", "state_id": "Canceled", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1785", "number": 1785, "title": "Try limiting same symbol tiles", "description": "We'll try limiting the same symbol tiles to see if we can overcome difficulty volatility and repeat tile mega tiles that way.", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": "2025-05-05T19:14:36Z", "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 408980, "labels": ["Puzzle Editor", "Improvement"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-28T15:26:29Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T19:14:36Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1692", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1804", "record": {"id": "ENG-1804", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Canceled", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1804", "number": 1804, "title": "Implement a fall back strategy if the tutorial couldn't find relevant highlighted object", "description": "We would try to cover those scenarios as much as we can. However, it would be great to have a fall back strategy for scenarios we couldn't test it out. So if any tutorial has a step to highlight an object or UI component that the component is missing, then implement the fall back as marking tutorial completed or putting \"tap anywhere to continue\" function with some delays. \n\nWith those method, we can cover all the tutorials broken based on the highlight problems. At least they won't create hard blocker for the player progression.", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": "2025-05-05T19:35:35Z", "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 408959, "labels": ["Tutorial Editor"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-30T18:10:17Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T19:35:35Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1694", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1806", "record": {"id": "ENG-1806", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_c77c50cc15c5342d", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1806", "number": 1806, "title": "Foresight above Tiles transparency implementation", "description": "![image.png]([URL_51534])\n\nI belive lexi has the foresite ability where she chooses a tile thats on a lower level and she sees what it is, but unfortunatley the tiles above will make hard to see what is it. So we choose to make them transparent for a few seconds and then back with full opacity.\n\n[foresiteTransparency_AllTiles001.webm]([URL_51533])\n\nTo achive this with all the tiles i had to modify a lot of materials and shader. Because unity has issues when we render transparent material objects on top of each other most of the time all the tiles will be like non transparent. opacue. Once a bool is true on the animator then it starts an animation swaping the material with a clone of the material but with transparent rendering method and animation of them going to semi-transparent happens.\n\nBecause we need to animate the shadow as well  so it doesnt go in the way of viewing whats under the tile i had to add animation to the shadow parent object and animating the shadow planes.\n\n![image.png]([URL_51532])\n\nBecause each tile is a bit different like the bundle tile , bomb etc, the animators that control the fading animations might be put on different parents so because of that please look up at the foresite debug UI button that i did in the foresite_transparency.unity scene to see what its trigged for each tile type. That button triggers all of the tiles at once. For example the bomb tile holds the animator with the transparent bool parameter right on the main game object.\n\nKeep in mind that the vanishing tile is a bit different because it has different states and colours. So i made in such way that it goes transparent evin from yellow/orange/red state.\n\nThis visual effect was hard to achive but i managed to solve yet another issue. Toxic Disolve. Before the tile was disolving when nathan was trowing the toxic bottle at it, but the new simbols like the fire and the key didnt disolved like the rest of the tile. So i fixed that. all you need to do is to activate the fade4good trigger in the fakeShadow animator component so we get rid of the shadow as well when we disolve the tile.\n\n[toxic_Disolve_Fixed001.webm]([URL_51531])\n\nI'm doing a PR right now but my branch is TilesShaderWork. I played a bit the levels and nothing seem to be broken. This things happen only when u trigger the bool trigger in the animator.\n\nIf you have any question please reach me on slack! Good luck with this implementation!", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-11-04T13:35:33Z", "completed_at": "2024-11-15T14:09:00Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 655525, "labels": ["VFX Integration", "Sprint 25 Destiny - Nov 8th", "Destiny"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-1702", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-10-31T19:17:23Z", "updated_at": "2024-11-15T14:09:00Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1698", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-181", "record": {"id": "ENG-181", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-181", "number": 181, "title": "Add Top Of Domino Marker In Puzzle Editor", "description": null, "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2023-09-19T16:32:54Z", "completed_at": "2023-10-02T16:11:55Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2024-04-03T00:47:40Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 1245802, "labels": ["Puzzle Editor", "Sprint 4 - September 29th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2023-09-06T19:09:16Z", "updated_at": "2023-10-02T16:11:55Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1700", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1811", "record": {"id": "ENG-1811", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_caafeec2804b3a67", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1811", "number": 1811, "title": "Tooltip and milestone texts are overlapping", "description": "Version or date: unity editor\n\n### Description: \n\nWhen there are more than 4 items in the win screen along with the milestone preview, their texts are overlapping. The tooltip texts are not readable anymore and the milestone text is above it. \n\n### Visual References:\n\n![image.png]([URL_51540])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to make the tooltip above for the items in the bottom row. \n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Play a level with many different rewards like the start of chapter 4 or 10 levelish chapter 3.\n2. Click on the item in the bottom middle\n\n##", "priority": 4, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-01-17T22:26:47Z", "completed_at": "2025-01-23T15:12:26Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 556102, "labels": ["Sprint 28 - January 17th", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-11-01T15:20:55Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-23T15:12:26Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1705", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1816", "record": {"id": "ENG-1816", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_PERSON_2218", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1816", "number": 1816, "title": "Rewinding quickly can cause sprite mismatch on the streak ability", "description": "Version or date: ios 269\n\n### Description:  \n\nIf the rewind is used too fast back and forth, the reward sprite might not be updated according to the current reward or so. The bar is also broken by showing the next streak bar rather than the actual one. \n\n### Visual References:\n\n[Record_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5870]_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.mp4]([URL_51552])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to make sure that the streak bar and the reward sprite is synced with the actual progression in levels.\n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Complete 4 and 5 streaks\n2. Complete the first 5 of the 6 streak\n3. Then match the last tile and ewind back and forth quickly\n4. Observe that the mismatch happens on both streak bars and its reward icons\n\n##", "priority": 4, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-12-16T16:40:01Z", "completed_at": "2025-01-09T16:11:55Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 576202, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-11-01T17:25:35Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-09T16:11:55Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1715", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1825", "record": {"id": "ENG-1825", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_8140f09bf9f1b94c", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1825", "number": 1825, "title": "Tutorial Editor Updates", "description": "The new tutorial editor updates, as discussed and decided in the meeting.", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-05-05T19:12:42Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 408982, "labels": ["Tutorial Editor"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-11-04T16:10:09Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T19:12:42Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1721", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1830", "record": {"id": "ENG-1830", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1825", "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_8140f09bf9f1b94c", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1830", "number": 1830, "title": "Implement the hand sprite", "description": "We will use the hand in the Tile Dozer game as another feature for the tutorial editor. It already has the sprite and the animation. It just needs to be integrated into the tutorial editor as an action, similar to the pointer arrow logic.", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-11-06T16:59:37Z", "completed_at": "2024-11-22T17:53:01Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 645221, "labels": [], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-11-04T16:10:09Z", "updated_at": "2024-11-22T17:53:01Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1724", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1833", "record": {"id": "ENG-1833", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1833", "number": 1833, "title": "Ipad Responsiveness Issues Updated List", "description": "* Touching in the middle of the Sophie image or various parts of the Sophie image on the character screen doesn\u2019t trigger going into individual characters\u2019 upgrade screen. Touch area needs to be expanded\n* The x button area for all pop-up offers are not responsive. You have to hit the bottom part of the x button\n* The highlight area of Sophie in tutorials are too small and barely covers Sophie\n* The quest arrow doesn\u2019t point the quest properly. The arrow is also too small. I didn\u2019t notice where I needed to click to continue. We just need to make all these highligted tutorial screen \u201ctap to continue\u201d so people don\u2019t get stuck.\n\nI don't have any repro steps for them because it doesn't create any of the problems in the editor and I don't have any ipad \ud83d\ude42 \n\nPlease reaach out to @Leonard for those issues.", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-05-05T19:35:28Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 408959, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-11-04T16:37:48Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T19:35:28Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1725", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1834", "record": {"id": "ENG-1834", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1812", "assignee_id": "usr_caafeec2804b3a67", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1834", "number": 1834, "title": "Collect & Win Event Issue List", "description": "Version or date: ios 281\n\n 1. ~~Clicking \u201clet\u2019s go\u201d button on magical wings doesn\u2019t close the pop-up (the first pop up shown automatically)~~\n\n    [RPReplay_Final1730527781.MP4]([URL_51572])\n 2. ~~If the first event level is not completed, the event is popping up every time saga map visited.~~\n    1. ~~The first event pop up has no target showing collect 0 tokens and 0/0.~~\n\n       [ScreenRecording_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5847]_1 (1).MOV]([URL_51545])\n 3. There is no pop up if the event is unlocked after ch3 lvl5. ~~This event is unlocked later on because it's not turned on for that week so I couldn't see any event pop up at where it should be.~~ \n    1. ~~Therefore, the events are unlocked in level so it creates a problem in the first 2 rewards based on syncing issues.~~\n\n       [WhatsApp Video 2024-11-04 at 19.44.30_b4bf090b.mp4]([URL_51571])\n\n       [WhatsApp Video 2024-11-04 at 19.43.38_b15c1be6.mp4]([URL_51570])\n 4. ~~The rewards are above the inventory.~~\n\n    ![Screenshot_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5871]-04_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.jpg]([URL_51569])\n 5. If there is a surplus token after completing a milestone, there is no additional vfx to show the next progression bar. \n\n    [RPReplay_Final1730476574.MP4]([URL_51544])\n 6. ~~In live ops, instead of Infinite rewind icon, it\u2019s showing regular rewind icon on reward screen.~~ \n\n    ![WhatsApp Image 2024-11-04 at 19.47.55_ad15dd3e.jpg]([URL_51568])\n 7. If the page is changed while getting an event reward, the circular progress bar stays as complete but the pop up progress is in the next reward milestone.  \n\n    [WhatsApp Video 2024-11-04 at 19.45.01_45205e02.mp4]([URL_51567])\n\n    [WhatsApp Video 2024-11-04 at 19.45.57_fb1732f8.mp4]([URL_51566])\n 8. If the scene is changed before getting event rewards, the rewards are suspended. The reward screen and animation is triggered after new tokens earned through levels. \n\n    [WhatsApp Video 2024-11-04 at 19.47.09_dd71f700.mp4]([URL_51565])\n    1. After getting new event milestone and starting a new session, the bar shows 7/7 but instead it's like 2/7. \n       1. If I change the scene, it corrects itself as 1/7\n\n          [WhatsApp Video 2024-11-04 at 19.47.29_b9de7a56.mp4]([URL_51564])\n 9. Should say \"Collect Ladybug Tokens by Beating Levels and Win Amazing Rewards!\"\n\n    ![image.png]([URL_51563])\n10. ~~If level is failed, the vfx is still triggered and tokens are floating to the progress bar.~~ \n\n[RPReplay_Final1733141438.MP4]([URL_51562])", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-12-04T17:37:59Z", "completed_at": "2024-12-23T12:25:14Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 600909, "labels": ["Nova Release", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-11-04T16:46:02Z", "updated_at": "2024-12-23T12:25:14Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1739", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1847", "record": {"id": "ENG-1847", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Canceled", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1847", "number": 1847, "title": "Ch2 Lvl 3 is scene is loaded twice", "description": "Version or date: android 343\n\n### Description: \n\nThere was a moment where I heard two click sound while clicking on the play button of that prelevel dialogue. But I couldn't record it. \n\nWhat's happening in that level is the tiles are loaded twice along with probably the scene because I'm hearing the game music on top of each other. Both levels are playable at the same time. \n\nI couldn't repro the issue but here is the log if that's helpful\n\n```\n[QualitySetter] detailedDeviceModel: OPPO CPH2205\n[QualitySetter] <color=green>Known device model: OPPO CPH2205 Quality medium </color>\n**ERROR**\nError during initialization of unity services: Some services couldn't be initialized. Look at inner exceptions to get more information.\n___ STACK ______\n<Start>d__11:MoveNext()\nSystem.Runtime.CompilerServices.AsyncTaskMethodBuilder`1:SetException(Exception)\nUnity.Services.Core.<InitializeAsync>d__15:MoveNext()\nSystem.Runtime.CompilerServices.AsyncTaskMethodBuilder`1:SetException(Exception)\nUnity.Services.Core.Internal.<InitializeAsync>d__19:MoveNext()\nSystem.Runtime.CompilerServices.AsyncTaskMethodBuilder`1:SetException(Exception)\nUnity.Services.Core.Internal.<InitializeServicesAsync>d__22:MoveNext()\nSystem.Runtime.CompilerServices.AsyncTaskMethodBuilder`1:SetException(Exception)\nUnity.Services.Core.Internal.<<InitializeServicesAsync>g__InitializePackagesAsync|1>d:MoveNext()\nSystem.Runtime.CompilerServices.AsyncTaskMethodBuilder`1:SetException(Exception)\nUnity.Services.Core.Internal.<InitializeRegistryAsync>d__3:MoveNext()\nSystem.Runtime.CompilerServices.AsyncTaskMethodBuilder`1:SetResult(TResult)\nUnity.Services.Core.Internal.<<InitializeRegistryAsync>g__TryInitializePackageAsync|0>d:MoveNext()\nSystem.