olor=#960018>GameEvents</color>\\] Could not find DominoHand. In both scenarios, and the earlier one is\n\n* \\[WorldMap\\] Save puzzle time<<Expensive call>>,\n\n* 4-14 not finished, 4-15 \\[<color=brown>Loading</color>\\] \\_puzzle: DominoSchema.Puzzle \\_puzzleId: 104 \\_chapter: 4 \\_level: 15 \\_levelName: 15\n* 5-9 & 5-10 \\[<color=brown>Loading</color>\\] \\_puzzle: DominoSchema.Puzzle \\_puzzleId: 129 \\_chapter: 5 \\_level: 10 \\_levelName: 10", "priority": 4, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": "2025-05-05T19:19:01Z", "archived_at": "2025-11-06T04:09:43Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 408975, "labels": ["Crashlytics", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2024-11-20T18:42:13Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T19:19:01Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1813", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1913", "record": {"id": "ENG-1913", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_PERSON_2218", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1913", "number": 1913, "title": "An app exception happenning on chapter 2 end screen while starting ch3 lvl 1", "description": "Chrashlytics Link:\n\nThe Script / Function: Init\n\n* NullReferenceException - Object reference not set to an instance of an object.\n* ChapterEndScreen\n* auto_awesome\n* Fresh issue\n\nFurther Detail: It happens twice. In both players, they played the ch2 lvl 20 twice and that bug happens after they started ch3 lvl1. And again, the last event for them is \\[<color=lime>Analytics</color>\\] TUTORIAL: |NateSelect_Hide Info_0|\n\nTwo different user story:\n\n[harmonygames.metabaseapp.com](https://harmonygames.metabaseapp.com/question?user_id=[IDENTIFIER_24661]&event_name=adjusting_quality_dynamically&event_is=#)\n\n[harmonygames.metabaseapp.com](https://harmonygames.metabaseapp.com/question?user_id=[IDENTIFIER_24660]&event_name=adjusting_quality_dynamically&event_is=#)", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-11-20T18:46:56Z", "completed_at": "2024-11-27T18:32:09Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-05-28T08:10:35Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 637982, "labels": ["Crashlytics", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2024-11-20T18:46:56Z", "updated_at": "2024-11-27T18:32:09Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1825", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1924", "record": {"id": "ENG-1924", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_caafeec2804b3a67", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1924", "number": 1924, "title": "Setting buttons for tile dozer and lucky drop are not correct", "description": "### Description: The setting buttons are added in both scene but the location is wrong. \n\n### Visual References: \n\n![Screenshot_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5901]-21_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.jpg]([URL_51667])\n\n![Screenshot_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5900]-87_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.jpg]([URL_51666])\n\n### Expected Outcome:\n\n![image.png]([URL_51665])", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-01-06T14:49:29Z", "completed_at": "2025-01-09T16:11:48Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 576202, "labels": ["Easy Fix - Just do it!", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-11-22T18:16:44Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-09T16:11:48Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1831", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-193", "record": {"id": "ENG-193", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-193", "number": 193, "title": "black rectangular rack on the main game for both iOS and AND", "description": null, "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2023-09-13T21:23:48Z", "completed_at": "2023-10-17T12:30:12Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2024-04-18T00:49:58Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 1224424, "labels": ["Friends & Family Build September"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2023-09-13T18:47:35Z", "updated_at": "2023-10-17T12:30:12Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1834", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1932", "record": {"id": "ENG-1932", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_Robert", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1932", "number": 1932, "title": "Automatically move player map token to next chapter when they complete the last level for the first time in current chapter.", "description": "Create this as a tutorial event in addition to just making it implemented across the entire game.\n\nSo the order of procedure is as follows:\n\n1) Player wins the level\n2) Chapter rewards granted or characters unlocked\n3) Or any other \"clean up\" type events (live ops, etc)\n4) Once that's all completed, automatically load the next chapter for the player with the saga map token on level 1.\n\n@julia.lawson please make sure that this does not interfere with our FTUE design especially the step where we educate the players on how to move around chapters via chapter selection button.", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-12-10T16:46:18Z", "completed_at": "2024-12-17T17:26:44Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 609248, "labels": ["Sprint 27 Nova - Dec 6th", "FTUE", "Nova Release"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-11-25T19:29:16Z", "updated_at": "2024-12-17T17:26:44Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1841", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1939", "record": {"id": "ENG-1939", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1939", "number": 1939, "title": "The red dot of character and minigame buttons are not displayed correctly", "description": "Version or date: ios 485\n\n### Description: \n\nThe red dot should be visible on char button if upgradeable characters are present. It should also be visible on minigame button if token count is equal or more than 50 or lives are ready for the other minigames. However, the red dot for both buttons are visible in general without satisfying any of those conditions. \n\nHOWEVER, both of the red dots behave correctly after unlocking the river tile or memory game minigames. Since they are in ready state even before unlocking them, the red dot gets visible. \n\nInterestingly, it also somehow makes char button red dot visible all the time. \n\n### Visual References:\n\n[RPReplay_Final1732670549.MP4]([URL_51683])\n\n[RPReplay_Final1732672442.MOV]([URL_51682])\n\n[RPReplay_Final1732672543.MP4]([URL_51681])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to ignore the ready state of minigames if they're not unlocked yet and make char red dot independent. \n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Observe the red dot behaviour until unlocking the minigames\n2. Unlock the river and memory tile \n3. Play both of them\n4. Observe the behavior again", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-12-02T18:36:16Z", "completed_at": "2024-12-16T08:37:51Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 611216, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-1904", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-11-27T17:06:41Z", "updated_at": "2024-12-16T08:37:51Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1851", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1948", "record": {"id": "ENG-1948", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1473", "assignee_id": "usr_bdf01b53c6a92c5e", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1948", "number": 1948, "title": "All Achievement Issues", "description": "Version or date: ios 500\n\n### Description: \n\n1. First of all, both quests and achievements are not visible once they section is unlocked.\n   1. I killed the app and restarted, they are populated in a second or so.\n\n      [RPReplay_Final1732752615 (1).MP4]([URL_51755])\n2. Rewarded gems are not synced with the back so the earned gems are gone in the next session\n\n   [chapter 1 achievement issue & gem not saved.mp4]([URL_51754])\n\n   .\n3. Match tiles achievement is hooked up to matching jumbo tiles. It only increases by matching jumbo ti\n\n   [match tile as match mega tile - Made with Clipchamp.mp4]([URL_51753])\n\n   les.\n4. The play minigames achievements are only claimable once all of the minigame achievements are achieved\n\n   [minigames - all or nothing.mp4]([URL_51752])\n\n   .\n5. Since the achievements are unlocked in the middle of the chapter 2, the achievements to collects stars from the chapter 1 still asking many starts to recollect.\n\n   [chapter 1 achievement issue.mp4]([URL_51751])\n6. I sometimes see where two of the same track achievements are visible simultaneously.\n\n   ![image.png]([URL_51700])\n7. Not Hooked Up Achievements\n   1. Buy 1 Item from the Shop\n   2. Change Your Player Name\n   3. Change Your Avatar\n   4. Claim 1 Rewarded Ad\n   5. Complete 1 Quest\n   6. Buy 1 Item from the Shop (both iap and items via gems etc)", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2024-12-10T20:10:28Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 619164, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-1969", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-11-28T11:05:42Z", "updated_at": "2024-12-10T20:10:28Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1856", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1952", "record": {"id": "ENG-1952", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_Robert", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1952", "number": 1952, "title": "Red Dot notification consistency", "description": "We need to make sure that the red dot is consistently placed in all places, and has the bouncing animation. Couple places right now that does not have a red dot and should:\n\n1) the \"weekly\" tab under quest. This possibly applies to the other quest tabs on that same screen as well. Please make sure they are animated with the bounce vfx.\n\n2) The hourly collection notification does not have the bounce\n\n3) The red dot on mini game does not have a bounce\n\n4) The placement of the notification for character profile button on home screen is different from other button's placement.\n\n5) The bounce notification VFX for the various bottom UI navigation button is inconsistent, sometimes some would animate, some wouldn't.\n\nWe should add placements of the red notification as well on the following places:\n\n1) When mini games have max tokens for lucky drop or tile dozer, it should have a red notification icon as well, top right of the frame.\n\n2) When there is a life to claim for river tile and memory tile, we should have a red notification icon, top right of frame as well.\n\n3) Under character selection screen, let's move the green upgrade arrow to the right end of the progress bar, and let's put a red notification dot for characters ready to be upgraded top right of the frame.", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-12-02T18:35:58Z", "completed_at": "2024-12-10T20:42:09Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 619132, "labels": ["Sprint 27 Nova - Dec 6th", "Nova Release", "Bug", "Improvement"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-11-29T22:23:59Z", "updated_at": "2024-12-10T20:42:09Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1859", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1955", "record": {"id": "ENG-1955", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-1834", "assignee_id": "usr_caafeec2804b3a67", "creator_id": "usr_63fffeb4fab5233e", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1955", "number": 1955, "title": "Remove ladybug animation after losing a level", "description": "'@Leonard said:\n\n> When you lose a level you still get a ladybug live ops flying animation after you quit the level. This is not correct behavior. We shouldn\u2019t show an animation. The counter doesn\u2019t go up though so that\u2019s good. @Samuel", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-12-04T17:38:01Z", "completed_at": "2024-12-11T17:49:10Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 617865, "labels": ["Sprint 27 Nova - Dec 6th", "Nova Release"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-12-01T16:48:21Z", "updated_at": "2024-12-11T17:49:10Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1869", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1964", "record": {"id": "ENG-1964", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1964", "number": 1964, "title": "Julius and Lexi didn't unlock at 4-15 and 5-25 respectively", "description": "Version or date: testflight ios 86\n\n### Description: \n\nIn [PERSON_NAME_0036]'s ftue, both julius and lexi didn't unlock when they are supposed to in the fixed levels. Lexi for 4-15, and Julius for 5-25 \n\n### Visual References:\n\n[RPReplay_Final1733144837.MP4]([URL_51765])\n\n[RPReplay_Final1733148043.MP4]([URL_51764])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to unlock both characters regardless of which FTUE at their respective levels\n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Play 4-15 and observe no lexi token\n2. Play 5-25 and observe no julius token", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2024-12-26T14:56:06Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 596438, "labels": ["Nova Release", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-12-02T14:53:11Z", "updated_at": "2024-12-26T14:56:06Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1875", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-197", "record": {"id": "ENG-197", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "creator_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-197", "number": 197, "title": "Define backend tech stack", "description": "Programming language: Python\n\nFramework: FastAPI", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2023-09-18T14:19:29Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 1266075, "labels": ["Server/Cloud", "Sprint 3 - September 15th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2023-09-18T14:19:29Z", "updated_at": "2023-09-18T14:19:48Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1886", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-198", "record": {"id": "ENG-198", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "creator_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-198", "number": 198, "title": "Kickoff API v1 implementation", "description": "Start API development using FastAPI: Project setup and scaffolding", "priority": 0, "estimate": 2, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2023-09-18T14:22:37Z", "completed_at": "2024-01-03T06:16:11Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 1112478, "labels": ["Server/Cloud", "Sprint 4 - September 29th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2023-09-18T14:22:23Z", "updated_at": "2024-01-03T06:16:11Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1890", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1983", "record": {"id": "ENG-1983", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1983", "number": 1983, "title": "Quests stays visually locked after getting unlocked in both FTUEs", "description": "Version or date: ios 571\n\n### Description: \n\nThe lock icon is persistent in the quest button while it's unlocked functionally. It sometimes show red dot sometimes lock symbol don't understand how it's caused. \n\n### Visual References: \n\n[RPReplay_Final1733495440.MP4]([URL_51794])\n\n[RPReplay_Final1733320193.MP4]([URL_51793])\n\n![image.png]([URL_51792])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to make it visually unlocked also. \n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Complete lvl 2-16", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2024-12-26T14:49:04Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 596445, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-12-04T16:12:03Z", "updated_at": "2024-12-26T14:49:04Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1893", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-1986", "record": {"id": "ENG-1986", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": null, "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-1986", "number": 1986, "title": "Nate's removal ability has no VFX on vanishing tiles", "description": "Version or date: ios 571\n\n### Description: \n\nRemoval ability of Nate has a dissolve VFX for regular tiles. However, it doesn't work on vanishing tiles. That's why it looks like there is a delay in the action - the vanishing tile stays for a while then disappear both functionally and visually\n\n### Visual References:\n\n[RPReplay_Final1733326428.MP4]([URL_51798])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to integrate dissolve VFX to vanishing tile as well.\n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Start a vanishing tile level with Nate\n2. Trigger his removal on vanishing tiles\n3. Observe that there is no vfx", "priority": 4, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-05-05T19:18:20Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 408976, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-12-04T16:23:02Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T19:18:20Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1897", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-199", "record": {"id": "ENG-199", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "creator_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-199", "number": 199, "title": "Setup backend infrastructure in AWS", "description": null, "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2024-01-03T06:54:13Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2024-07-04T01:32:24Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 1112440, "labels": ["Server/Cloud"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2023-09-18T14:24:04Z", "updated_at": "2024-01-03T06:54:13Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1909", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-200", "record": {"id": "ENG-200", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "creator_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-200", "number": 200, "title": "Define data structure", "description": null, "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2024-01-03T06:54:10Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2024-07-04T01:32:24Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 1112440, "labels": ["Server/Cloud", "Data"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2023-09-18T14:24:41Z", "updated_at": "2024-01-03T06:54:10Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1910", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2000", "record": {"id": "ENG-2000", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_bdf01b53c6a92c5e", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2000", "number": 2000, "title": "Quests sometimes are not populated once they are unlocked", "description": "Version or date: android 772 and ios 626\n\n### Description: \n\nQuests sometimes unlocked pretty good but sometimes not.\n\nWhen they doesn't populate properly, \n\n1. the lock icon stays\n2. both quests and achievements are not populated\n3. achievements (other than collect stars from chapter, and match tiles)\n\nRestarting the app populates both. The non counted achievements starts to count afterwards.  \n\n### Visual References:\n\n[VID-20241211-WA0010.mp4]([URL_51822])\n\n[quest not populated - Made with Clipchamp.mp4]([URL_51821])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to populate them no matter what. \n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Play until 2-1 is completed\n2. Use non-steady network\n3. Observe that quests are not unlocked properly", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-12-26T14:55:51Z", "completed_at": "2025-01-03T15:43:41Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 584871, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-2012", "type": "relates"}, {"target": "ENG-1977", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-12-11T17:31:54Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-03T15:43:41Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1915", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2005", "record": {"id": "ENG-2005", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_8140f09bf9f1b94c", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2005", "number": 2005, "title": "Tutorial Editor Can Play Sound Files On a Seperate Event", "description": "Right now our tutorial editor can play sound files as a part of the \"Show Message\" event. Please make it so that sounds can be played without using a text book as a well as a separate event.", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2024-12-13T17:32:19Z", "completed_at": "2024-12-30T12:11:12Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 590843, "labels": ["Tutorial Editor"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-12-13T17:31:35Z", "updated_at": "2024-12-30T12:11:12Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1920", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-201", "record": {"id": "ENG-201", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "creator_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-201", "number": 201, "title": "Define data storages source", "description": "RDS, DynamoDB, S3", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2024-03-04T17:55:52Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2024-09-05T02:27:19Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 1023938, "labels": ["Server/Cloud", "Data"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2023-09-18T14:29:19Z", "updated_at": "2024-03-04T17:55:52Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1922", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2011", "record": {"id": "ENG-2011", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_bdf01b53c6a92c5e", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2011", "number": 2011, "title": "Daily Login Issues List", "description": "Version or date: iOS_662 & android_789\n\n### Description: \n\n1. The daily login pops up without waiting for the saga map. It suddenly pops up in both the loading screen and the board scene.\n   1. It should be queued like every other pop up in the saga map. Ask @[PERSON_NAME_0092] for further details on that. \n\n      [Record_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5948]_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.mp4]([URL_51837])", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-01-10T15:26:49Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 574807, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-2006", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-12-16T16:41:49Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-10T15:26:49Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1926", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2015", "record": {"id": "ENG-2015", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_63fffeb4fab5233e", "state_id": "Canceled", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2015", "number": 2015, "title": "Capture additional data in left_level analytics event", "description": "We need to capture \n\n1- <ms> Max streak - what\u2019s the max streak players have achieved in a level, this will go in as ms in left_level. Max streak is defined as \"max number of uninterrupted matches a player did in a level\"\n\n2- <dp> Difficulty paramaters - \\[# of chops default, # of effective chops after dynamic difficulty is applied, # of unique symbols\\]", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": "2025-05-05T19:09:56Z", "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 408984, "labels": ["Nova Release", "Data"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-12-18T06:28:05Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T19:09:56Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1930", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2019", "record": {"id": "ENG-2019", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_63fffeb4fab5233e", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2019", "number": 2019, "title": "Implement Gacha Chest", "description": "We want to implement a gacha chest.\n\nWe'll add a cool icon on the right hand side that indicates this is the button to summon hero tokens. It will open up a hero summon page with a hero chest. When summoned, we'll show the quest chest animation. When hero is summoned, it will give the following items\n\n1 pull = 1 hero token, costs 30 gems\n\n10 pull = 10 hero tokens, 270 gems\n\nAll unlocked heroes have equal drop rate at each pull. For instance, if you have 2 characters Sophie and Nathan unlocked only and you do a 10 pull, you will get \\~5 Sophie, \\~5 Nathan tokens.\n\nThe icon gets unlocked after character upgrade tutorial.\n\nWe could use same chest sparkles we have from quest chests and their opening animation for these chests.\n\nWe could use the same SFX as we used in the quest page.\n\nWe also need analytics tracking, that can be tied to `shop_purchase` event. Please define a new category called tavern where quantity is 1 or 10 depending on the type of chest they open (onepull vs tenpull)\n\n![image.png]([URL_51857])\n\n![image.png]([URL_51856])\n\n![image.png]([URL_51855])\n\n![image.png]([URL_51854])\n\nFigma link is here: \n\n[Figma: The Collaborative Interface Design Tool]([URL_51853])", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-01-16T18:15:14Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 565999, "labels": ["Nova Release"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-12-18T21:02:26Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-16T18:15:14Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1931", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-202", "record": {"id": "ENG-202", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "creator_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "state_id": "Canceled", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-202", "number": 202, "title": "Implement CI/CD code pipeline", "description": null, "priority": 4, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": "2024-03-18T18:33:45Z", "archived_at": "2024-09-19T02:55:41Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 1003741, "labels": ["Server/Cloud"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2023-09-18T14:30:00Z", "updated_at": "2024-03-18T18:33:45Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1939", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2027", "record": {"id": "ENG-2027", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_bdf01b53c6a92c5e", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2027", "number": 2027, "title": "Leaderboard Client Issues", "description": "Version or date: ios 812\n\n### Description: \n\n* Chests have no tooltip to show the rewards.\n* Relegation zone is visible in bronze league in which there is no other league to relegate \n\n  [ScreenRecording_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_5963]_1.MP4]([URL_51868])\n* Promotion zone is visible in king league in which there is no other league to promote\n* The rewards presented are not fitting well to phone frames.\n  * It should be in 2 rows with balanced amount of icons in both rows.\n\n    ![image.png]([URL_51867])\n  * \"Leftover Tokens\" should be changed into \"Leftover Tiles\"\n\n    ![image.png]([URL_51866])", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-01-08T13:15:38Z", "completed_at": "2025-01-20T14:20:13Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 560474, "labels": ["Sprint 28 - January 17th", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2024-12-27T15:24:53Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-20T14:20:13Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1942", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-203", "record": {"id": "ENG-203", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "creator_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-203", "number": 203, "title": "Analytics with Google's BigQuery", "description": null, "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2024-03-04T17:55:57Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2024-09-05T02:27:19Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 1023938, "labels": ["Server/Cloud"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2023-09-18T14:30:21Z", "updated_at": "2024-03-04T17:55:57Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1970", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2056", "record": {"id": "ENG-2056", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_bdf01b53c6a92c5e", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2056", "number": 2056, "title": "Quests are not refreshed in dev environment", "description": "Version or date: ios 942\n\n### Description: \n\nThe quests are not refreshed in dev environment -\n\nmy earlier progress is saved into later days for both daily and weekly quests. \n\n### Visual References: \n\n[ScreenRecording_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6012]_1.MP4]([URL_51965])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to refresh the quests and its individual progress in every day and week depending on which type of quests. \n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Make some progression\n2. Wait for the next day and week\n3. Observe they didn't get refreshed.", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-01-16T17:38:09Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 566036, "labels": ["Bug", "Sprint 29 Avengers -  January 31st"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-01-13T14:46:21Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-16T17:38:09Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1974", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-206", "record": {"id": "ENG-206", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "EPI-3", "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_Robert", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-206", "number": 206, "title": "Mini Game Starting Spawn Tiles Bug Fix", "description": "Currently the tiles at the very beginning are spawned based on BOTH symbols on the tile in hand. However this creates a problem since only HALF of the tile in hand is visible and can be matched. If the players are unlucky (50% of the time), the spawning tiles will be based off the non eligible half in hand, and causes a bunch of unmatchable tiles to spawn at the start. This is a bug.", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2023-10-31T08:38:23Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 1204496, "labels": ["Sprint 4 - September 29th", "Mini Game"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2023-09-19T01:30:37Z", "updated_at": "2023-10-31T08:38:23Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1979", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2064", "record": {"id": "ENG-2064", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2064", "number": 2064, "title": "Icon Management System", "description": "'@julia.lawson to fill up \n\nThe Icon Management System in very simple terms in a \"queue manager for the live ops icon\". The documentation for the system can be found here: \n\n[[URL_51975])\n\nAs a quick rundown, the system determines the following: \n\n* The number of icons on a scene\n* When they will appear whether locked or unlocked\n* What side of the screen will an icon appear\u00a0\n* In what order an icon will appear\u00a0\n* When will the icon disappear and/or change places\u00a0\n* The various elements on the icon like time, buttons, notifications, etc.\u00a0\n* Seasonal changes", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-01-27T17:34:59Z", "completed_at": "2025-02-10T12:16:59Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-11-06T04:09:45Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 530357, "labels": ["Avengers", "Sprint 29 Avengers -  January 31st"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-01-16T18:55:12Z", "updated_at": "2025-02-10T12:16:59Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1980", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2065", "record": {"id": "ENG-2065", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2065", "number": 2065, "title": "River Rush - Fastest Completion Event", "description": "The spec is ready for the mine rush. \n\n[\\[Live Ops\\] River Rush - Fastest Completion]([URL_51978])\n\nHere is the game references and wireframes. \n\n[Fastest Completion Event]([URL_51977])\n\n![River Rush.png]([URL_51976])", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-02-13T22:09:18Z", "completed_at": "2025-03-18T16:27:17Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-09-19T02:27:08Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 478267, "labels": ["Cappadocia", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-01-16T18:57:26Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-18T16:27:17Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1982", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2067", "record": {"id": "ENG-2067", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2067", "number": 2067, "title": "Weekly Leagues Bot Score Algorithm", "description": "Link to the Bot Score Algorithm\n\n[[URL_51980])\n\nHere is the starting parameters for Weekly Leagues\n\n[[URL_51979])", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-05-05T09:39:49Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-11-06T04:09:46Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 409554, "labels": ["Cappadocia", "Bot", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-2074", "type": "relates"}, {"target": "ENG-2111", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-01-16T19:05:30Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T09:39:49Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/1993", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2077", "record": {"id": "ENG-2077", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-2072", "assignee_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Bugs", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2077", "number": 2077, "title": "The level section in profiles doesn't show the total number of levels completed", "description": "The level box in players' profile through leaderboard doesn't show what is actually meant. It should show total number of levels beaten like in the all time list. \n\nReal player profiles doesn't show the total levels beaten in \"level\" section.\n\n* It doesn't work for weekly bots as well.\n* Even my own profile through the leaderboard doesn't show the correct amount here like it should be in my profile page. \n\n[Record_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6023]_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.mp4]([URL_51991])", "priority": 4, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 564751, "labels": ["DD 2.1"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-01-17T15:03:05Z", "updated_at": "2025-10-27T14:01:42Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2003", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2086", "record": {"id": "ENG-2086", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-2048", "assignee_id": "usr_PERSON_2218", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2086", "number": 2086, "title": "Win Streak Event icon isn't visible until their animation starts", "description": "UPDATED ISSUE\n\nThere is only win streak event icon that doesn't appear on the saga map directly as opposed to other icons. \n\n---\n\n[ScreenRecording_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6024]_1.MP4]([URL_51993])\n\n---\n\nVersion or date: ios 996\n\n### Description: \n\nThe events and their icons are strictly tied to each other. And the queue manager is making them disappear while waiting for the relevant animation to start. \n\n### Visual References:\n\n[invisible event icons - Made with Clipchamp.mp4]([URL_51992])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to show icons regardless of in which queue is the event is. \n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Play any level after 3-6\n2. Observe that both win&collect and win streak event icons are invisible until their animations are triggered.", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-01-21T17:54:28Z", "completed_at": "2025-01-29T14:18:17Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 547516, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-01-20T17:11:54Z", "updated_at": "2025-01-29T14:18:17Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2023", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2103", "record": {"id": "ENG-2103", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-2066", "assignee_id": "usr_PERSON_2218", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Canceled", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2103", "number": 2103, "title": "River Rush Events Debugger Client Side", "description": "The event is not ready yet, not started as well. It would be only reset the event duration as well as forcing bot to win so that I don't need to wait for them to finish to test losing scenarios. \n\n* Manipulating session timer\n* Enabling the event\n* Force bots to win", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": "2025-05-05T09:40:13Z", "archived_at": "2025-11-06T04:09:46Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 409554, "labels": ["Cappadocia", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-01-23T15:17:59Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T09:40:13Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2031", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2110", "record": {"id": "ENG-2110", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-2128", "assignee_id": "usr_caafeec2804b3a67", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Bugs", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2110", "number": 2110, "title": "Finish Memory Tile Quests count as 2", "description": "Version or date: android submission 133\n\n### Description: \n\nFinish Memory Tile quests counts as 2 after finishing them. It happens for both of the quests below in the reference video. \n\n```\nFinish Memory Tile in Any Mode 5 Times\n\nFinish Memory Tile in Hard Mode 3 Times\n```\n\nI noticed the issue after those are counted as 2 then started to record. \n\n### Visual References:\n\n[Record_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6040]_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.mp4]([URL_52013])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to count those quests by 1 instead of 2. \n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Check quests if there is any finish memory tile quest exists\n2. Check for its counter\n3. Finish in hard mode once\n4. Observe that it counts as 2.", "priority": 4, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 552869, "labels": ["Bug", "Pupusa"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-01-24T15:49:27Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T19:02:20Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2034", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2113", "record": {"id": "ENG-2113", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_caafeec2804b3a67", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2113", "number": 2113, "title": "Daily & Weekly Quests are not Reset for the current week", "description": "Version or date: ios 115 & android 133\n\n### Description: \n\nWhen I waited for the quests to be refreshed for the next week in live builds, they did not refresh. \n\nFor **ios**, I played in the weekend without any problem with the account I signed in. Then on Monday, both daily and weekly quests are not refreshed. \n\n* In daily quests, there are already completed quests with no progression on the key points. \n\n![image.png]([URL_52017])\n\n* In weekly quests, there are also completed quests with no key points, I just logged in. The chest progression is also not reset so if I collect 60 keys, I couldn't open the new chests. \n\n![image.png]([URL_52016])\n\nFor **android**, I played in the weekend without any problem with the account I signed in. Then on Monday, my chest progression and chest status are reset but there are 2 completed quests in each tab which makes it harder to claim chests. \n\n[1000001997 (1).mp4]([URL_52015])\n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Unlock quests\n2. Make progression on both daily and weekly\n3. Claim the chests \n4. Wait for the next week\n5. Observe that the status of quests and chests might not be refreshed.", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-01-30T17:33:48Z", "completed_at": "2025-02-24T16:52:45Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 509922, "labels": ["Avengers", "Bug", "Sprint 29 Avengers -  January 31st"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-01-27T16:22:17Z", "updated_at": "2025-02-24T16:52:45Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2039", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2119", "record": {"id": "ENG-2119", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "creator_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2119", "number": 2119, "title": "Explore Match Factory team's features", "description": null, "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-03-24T17:40:24Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 469554, "labels": ["Server/Cloud"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-01-27T17:36:00Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-24T17:40:24Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2058", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2137", "record": {"id": "ENG-2137", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_caafeec2804b3a67", "creator_id": "usr_fc22d5941b2aeb5c", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2137", "number": 2137, "title": "Adding the Win-Streak boosters to Fail/Quit Screens", "description": "We'll add the Win-Streak booster to the Fail/Quit Flow.\nIn both flows, we'll add the Win-Streak icon to the panel where we display Event tokens. The user will only see the Win-Streak stage they are currently in. The Win-Streak booster icon will appear first in the panel's order.\n\n![image.png]([URL_52061])", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-02-28T15:22:29Z", "completed_at": "2025-03-11T12:52:01Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-09-12T02:26:46Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 488562, "labels": ["Cappadocia", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-02-10T11:14:06Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-11T12:52:01Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2065", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2143", "record": {"id": "ENG-2143", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2143", "number": 2143, "title": "Unlock texts stays visible after unlocking the events", "description": "Version or date:\n\n### Description: \n\nUnlock texts stays visible after unlocking the events.\u00a0 \n\n* Nate's treasure hunt unlock text at first gets invisible but after the timer is visible it returns.\n\n### Visual References:\n\n![IMG_1536.PNG]([URL_52068])\n\n![IMG_1539.PNG]([URL_52067])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to hide those texts after level 3-5 which unlocks both events. \n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Reach 3-6\n2. Observe that the texts stays", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-02-11T23:21:11Z", "completed_at": "2025-02-12T14:16:39Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 527358, "labels": ["Avengers", "Bug", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-02-11T15:28:11Z", "updated_at": "2025-02-12T14:16:39Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2071", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2149", "record": {"id": "ENG-2149", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Todo", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2149", "number": 2149, "title": "Chapter reward boosters are not obtained in the first level of next chapters.", "description": "Version or date: Dev_iOS_1133\n\n### Description: \n\nChapter rewards are not obtained in the very next level in the next chapter. The chapter rewards and boosters are saved and synced after a level completion so those rewards are not obtained both functionally and visually.  \n\n### Visual References:\n\n[ScreenRecording_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6059]_1.MP4]([URL_52076])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to sync player data and show the active boosters in the prelevel dialogue along with the functionality. \n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Complete a chapter\n2. Earn the chapter rewards\n3. Wait for the next chapter to be loaded\n4. Observe that prelevel dialogue shows no active timed boosters\n5. Observe that in the gameplay those boosters are also not functionally active.", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 377932, "labels": ["DD 2.1", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-02-12T14:40:20Z", "updated_at": "2025-10-27T14:16:08Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2075", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2152", "record": {"id": "ENG-2152", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Canceled", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2152", "number": 2152, "title": "The quit flow should cover win streak booster as well", "description": "Version or date: Dev_iOS_1133\n\n### Description: \n\nThe new quit flow has some confirmatory pop ups along with some visuals. To make the level loss more impactful, we need to put \"You're win streak is about to end if you lose the level\" in there to increase the pressure on players' end. \n\nAsk @[PERSON_NAME_0092] about how it should be implemented. But as I saw it would be implemented in the 2nd pop up like you will lose by using the win streak pillow icons. \n\n### Visual References:\n\n[Record_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6062]_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4 (1).mp4]([URL_52082])\n\n![image (18).png]([URL_52081])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to implement the quit flow for both quitting through settings and to the out of moves flow. \n\n### Steps to Repro:", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": "2025-02-12T15:28:43Z", "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 527286, "labels": ["Cappadocia", "Bug", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-2137", "type": "duplicates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-02-12T15:24:31Z", "updated_at": "2025-02-12T15:29:00Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2083", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2160", "record": {"id": "ENG-2160", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_bdf01b53c6a92c5e", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2160", "number": 2160, "title": "First Try Event Minor Issues", "description": "Version or date: Dev_iOS_1169, Dev_Android_1305\n\n### Description: \n\n* The first try event is not implemented to the queue manager which can interrupt tutorial or other event flows.\n* The first try event is not implemented to the icon management. After 4-day quest is gone, it stays in the 4th spot with apparent gap.\n\n[Record_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6074]_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.mp4]([URL_52099])\n\n* [ENG-2161](https://linear.app/harmonygames-games/issue/ENG-2161/first-try-button-doesnt-direct-me-to-the-prelevel-dialogue-for-the)\n* Already-completed levels can still affect the first try event\n  * Beating the repeat levels increases both the multiplier and the event token count in the leaderboard.\n  * Similarly, losing a repeat level can reset the multiplier to 0.\n  * Don't know if it's expected but normally we shouldn't count any win or loss in repeat levels. \n\n[Record_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6073]_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.mp4]([URL_52098])\n\n* The multiplier animation going from 6x to 10x shouldn\u2019t play if you already reached at 10x. It shows 6x->10x even if you are at 10x already.", "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-02-18T11:59:20Z", "completed_at": "2025-02-18T16:57:57Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 518556, "labels": ["Cappadocia", "Bug", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-02-14T11:02:38Z", "updated_at": "2025-02-18T16:57:57Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2096", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2173", "record": {"id": "ENG-2173", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-2139", "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_8140f09bf9f1b94c", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2173", "number": 2173, "title": "Implement Bots", "description": "Make the event use bots. \n\n@douglas This is the part we need your help from. Can you create a ticket for yourself accordingly?", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-03-17T16:24:29Z", "completed_at": "2025-03-18T16:24:22Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-09-19T02:27:07Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 478270, "labels": ["Cappadocia", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-02-18T18:42:08Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-18T16:24:22Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2105", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2181", "record": {"id": "ENG-2181", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Bugs", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2181", "number": 2181, "title": "Leaderboard profile frames are visually different at first", "description": "Version or date: android 1335\n\n### Description: \n\nWhen I open the leaderboard, the bots' frames are bigger and different at first then it correct itself. \n\nThe weekly leaderboard player prefab is bigger first then shrink to its original scale.\n\n### Visual References:\n\n[ScreenRecording_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6092]_1.MP4]([URL_52121])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to show the correct frames without the bigger verison\n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Unlock leaderboard\n2. Open the leaderboard\n3. Observe that the bots' frames are bigger at first then it returns to its original scale and visual.", "priority": 4, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 517143, "labels": ["DD 2.1", "Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-02-19T16:30:48Z", "updated_at": "2025-10-27T13:55:48Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2111", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2187", "record": {"id": "ENG-2187", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_63fffeb4fab5233e", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2187", "number": 2187, "title": "Adjust +2 Wild-Tile at Start Booster to +1 Wild-Tile at Start", "description": "**Description:**\nModify the **pre-level booster** that grants **+2 wild tiles at the start** to now grant **+1 wild tile at the start**, which will be placed **randomly into the player\u2019s hand**.\n\n**Changes Required:**\n\n* Update the boost logic to provide **+1 wild tile instead of +2** at the start of the level.\n* Request a **new icon and in-game tile** from **Martin** to visually distinguish this boost from the **in-level wild tile boost**.\n* Update all references of **Start2WildTile** across all UI elements (Shop, Chapter Rewards, Live Ops Rewards, Chest Rewards) to **Start1WildTile** and ensure the correct new icon is used.\n* Update the golden tile in Win-Streak booster to diamond tile\n\n# Don't forget to update icons in the level fail prelevel dialogue as well. \n\nGold Tiles (which should be kept as is)\n\n* In-game gold tile boost\n  * every UI related to that as rewards such as\n    * chest tooltips\n    * rewards from tile dozer and lucky drop \n* Julius gold tile conversion ability\n* Store items with gold tile in-game boost (the left container)\n\nDiamond Tiles (change those gold tiles to diamond in both gameplay and UI)\n\n* Sophie's favor\n* Sophie's 5-streak ability after level 20\n* Nate's 6-streak ability after level 1\n* Nate's at start ability after level 40\n* Win & collect reward\n* The quest chest tooltip of 4th weekly chest\n* And any other timed gold tile reward\n* And any other shop items in timed boost container (which is usually middle or right container)", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-03-04T19:21:15Z", "completed_at": "2025-03-12T14:58:30Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-09-13T02:26:34Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 486996, "labels": ["Cappadocia", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-02-20T22:33:57Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-12T14:58:30Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2112", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2188", "record": {"id": "ENG-2188", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_63fffeb4fab5233e", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2188", "number": 2188, "title": "Update Pre-Level Booster - Hand Tile Boost Adjustment", "description": "**Description:**\nModify the **pre-level booster** that grants **+3 hand tiles at the start** to now grant **+1 hand tile at the start**.\n\n**Changes Required:**\n\n* Update the boost logic to provide **+1 hand tile instead of +3** at the start of the level.\n* Update all references of **Start3Tile** across all UI elements (Shop, Chapter Rewards, Live Ops Rewards, Chest Rewards) to **Start1Tile** and ensure the correct new icon is used.\n\nThese adjustments will rebalance pre-level boosters while ensuring visual clarity and consistency across the game.", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-03-04T19:21:19Z", "completed_at": "2025-03-12T14:58:35Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-09-13T02:26:34Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 486996, "labels": ["Cappadocia", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-02-20T22:34:55Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-12T14:58:35Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2114", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-219", "record": {"id": "ENG-219", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ART-259", "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_Robert", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-219", "number": 219, "title": "Glossy-ness of tiles", "description": "We want our tiles to be glossier. Both the corners and the symbols, so they start to resemble what we see in Domino Dreams and Domino Go. Plan is to have @Blake take lead and work with some shaders, once we have the Unity settings defined, we can supplement any additional required effort from the art side.\n\n![image.png]([URL_49904])", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2024-01-03T07:00:42Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 1112434, "labels": ["Improvement", "Main Game"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2023-09-22T00:07:10Z", "updated_at": "2024-01-03T07:00:42Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2126", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-220", "record": {"id": "ENG-220", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-11", "assignee_id": "usr_Robert", "creator_id": "usr_Robert", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-220", "number": 220, "title": "End Game Button", "description": "When players run out of cards, an \"end game\" button needs to appear that allows players to exit. In the final build there will be an \"exit\" funnel meaning a prompt asking players \"are you sure you want to quit because you might be losing so and so?\"\n\nWe should construct this 2 step funnel but leave it so we can customize the messaging in the prompt and tie it to a live ops event or some quest or some game state such as coins given up, character tokens given up, etc.", "priority": 4, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2023-09-29T17:25:30Z", "completed_at": "2024-03-06T00:36:57Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 1022097, "labels": ["Improvement", "Main Game"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2023-09-22T00:23:10Z", "updated_at": "2024-03-06T00:36:57Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2128", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2201", "record": {"id": "ENG-2201", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_49b9dfa5208d400d", "creator_id": "usr_c77c50cc15c5342d", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2201", "number": 2201, "title": "Streak Fever in-game Icon animation implementation", "description": "[StreakFeverSimb001.mp4]([URL_52154])\n\nWe have a prefab StreakFever_Simbol_Collect that we want to appear on top of the last matched tile of the streak and it will display a number and the icon. Please talk with @julia.lawson about the number amount.\n\n[[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6105].6115718.mp4]([URL_52153])\n\nThe prefab. should be above the tiles a bit\n\n![image.png]([URL_52152])\n\nPlease keep in mind that the amount it's made from two fonts and we need to change them both, if the amounts are fixed we should make a pool with them and just hide and unhide the ones we need.\n\nThis prefab its not ui stuff it lives in the 3d world on the board with the tiles.\n\nThe scene name is: Board_StreakFever_Simbol.unity and my branch is Marcus/Streak-Fever_Vfx\n\nI'm going to do a PR now.\n\nif you have any other questions shout out at me.\n\nGood luck!", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-03-18T16:24:36Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 478270, "labels": ["VFX Integration"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-03-04T18:03:28Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-18T16:24:36Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2129", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2202", "record": {"id": "ENG-2202", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": null, "creator_id": "usr_PERSON_2218", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2202", "number": 2202, "title": "Teams in saga map (UI only)", "description": "Move mini games to top hud.\n\nAdd new button on bottom hud.\n\nTeam Document: [[URL_52159])\n\nLives Bank Document: [[URL_52158])\n\nMiro Board: [[URL_52157])\n\nFigma: [[URL_52156])\n\n![image_from_clipboard.png]([URL_52155])", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-06-16T12:11:13Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-12-17T04:38:30Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 348923, "labels": ["Teams", "Cookie"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-03-04T22:59:16Z", "updated_at": "2025-06-16T12:11:13Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2137", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-221", "record": {"id": "ENG-221", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "creator_id": "usr_cc3e90160f490686", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-221", "number": 221, "title": "Add Interrupts Back Into Puzzle Editor", "description": null, "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2023-09-27T20:58:32Z", "completed_at": "2023-10-02T16:11:51Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2024-04-03T00:47:41Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 1245802, "labels": ["Sprint 4 - September 29th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2023-09-22T00:31:02Z", "updated_at": "2023-10-02T16:11:51Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2138", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2210", "record": {"id": "ENG-2210", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_PERSON_2218", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2210", "number": 2210, "title": "Teams leaderboard support (UI only)", "description": "Create the new Teams tab and both worldwide and local sections.\nCreate the team item.\nUse leaderboard code as reference.\n\nTeam Document: [[URL_52159])\n\nLives Bank Document: [[URL_52158])\n\nMiro Board: [[URL_52157])\n\nFigma: [[URL_52156])\n\n![image_from_clipboard.png]([URL_52176])", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-06-16T12:10:58Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-12-17T04:38:29Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 348923, "labels": ["Teams", "Cookie"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-03-04T23:54:03Z", "updated_at": "2025-06-16T12:10:58Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2143", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2215", "record": {"id": "ENG-2215", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_63fffeb4fab5233e", "creator_id": "usr_63fffeb4fab5233e", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2215", "number": 2215, "title": "Test Plan to Optimize the Base Pity Mechanic", "description": "### **Test Plan to Optimize the Base Pity Mechanic**\n\nSince we're establishing a **baseline with no pity mechanic**, we'll first analyze **win rates without any pity adjustments** and then optimize the **base pity mechanic**.\n\n## **1. Test Conditions**\n\nWe will run simulations for **Chapter 5, Levels 1-15**, under different **pity mechanic configurations**.\n\n### **Baseline Condition (No Pity Mechanic)**\n\n* **Goal:** Establish the **raw win rate** without any pity influence.\n* **Test Runs:** **7,500 bot plays (500 per level)**.\n* **Other Constants:**\n  * **Character:** Sophie (Level 10)\n  * **No adjustments** to **unique symbols, chops, or starting hand tiles**.\n  * **No win streaks, no pre-level boosters**.\n\n#### **Metrics to Record:**\n\n* **Attempts**\n* **Losses**\n* **Avg Win Rate**\n* **Avg Handtiles Left When Won**\n* **How Many Board Tiles Left When Lost**\n* **# of Tiles on the Board at Start**\n* **# of Tiles on the Starting Draw Pile**\n* **Avg Additional Tiles to finish the level when lost**\n\n### **Test Variations for Base Pity Mechanic**\n\nOnce the baseline is set, we will optimize these **base pity mechanic parameters**:\n\n```\n{0.0f, 0.1f, 0.16f, 0.26f, 0.41f, 0.66f, 1.0f}\n```\n\n* **Goal:** Determine the best sequence of pity activations.\n* **Variations:** Adjust **each probability in the range** to fine-tune the balance.\n\n#### **Test Cases**\n\nEach bot will:\n\n1. **Play without a pity mechanic (baseline test).**\n2. **Play with different base pity mechanic variations.**\n3. **Log key win/loss metrics.**\n\n---\n\n## **2. Optimization Strategy**\n\nOnce data is collected:\n\n1. **Compare baseline win rates to pity-adjusted win rates.**\n2. **Use Bayesian Optimization** to find the best pity mechanic activation sequence.\n3. \\*\\*Validate the final settings in a second simulation batch.\n\n---\n\n## **3. Running Bayesian Optimization to Determine Optimal Pity Mechanic Parameters**\n\nSince **Bayesian Optimization (BO)** is well-suited for optimizing **multi-variable functions** with expensive evaluations (such as bot simulations), we will use it to **find the best pity mechanic parameters** for *Domino Delights*.\n\n### **1. Problem Setup**\n\nWe need to **find the optimal pity mechanic settings** that:\n\n\u2705 Keep the **win rate in the target range (based on the level's base win rate)**.\n\n\u2705 Ensure a **near-miss experience** by adjusting **pity activation probabilities**.\n\n### **Parameters to Optimize**\n\nBayesian Optimization will **fine-tune the pity probabilities**:\n\n| **Pull Number** | **Current Pity Activation (Baseline)** | **Optimization Range** |\n| -- | -- | -- |\n| **1st** | 0.0f | Fixed (No pity on first pull) |\n| **2nd** | 0.1f | `[0.05 - 0.2]` |\n| **3rd** | 0.16f | `[0.1 - 0.3]` |\n| **4th** | 0.26f | `[0.15 - 0.4]` |\n| **5th** | 0.41f | `[0.25 - 0.55]` |\n| **6th** | 0.66f | `[0.5 - 0.85]` |\n| **7th** | 1.0f | Fixed (Always guarantees a match) |\n\nWe use **Bayesian Optimization** to efficiently explore these **parameters** and find the best configuration.\n\n### **2. Bayesian Optimization Approach**\n\nBayesian Optimization will:\n\n1. **Select an initial set of pity mechanic settings** and simulate win rates.\n2. **Use Gaussian Processes (GPs)** to predict the best parameters for the next simulation.\n3. **Iteratively refine the parameters** to find the optimal pity settings.\n\n#### **Objective Function**\n\nThe **objective function minimizes the absolute difference** from the **target win rate per level**:\n\ntotal_loss = \\\\sum |Simulated Win Rate - Base Win Rate of Level| / 15\n\nLower values are better.\n\n---\n\n## **4. Implementing Bayesian Optimization in Python**\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport skopt\nfrom skopt import gp_minimize\nfrom skopt.space import Real\nfrom skopt.utils import use_named_args\nimport pandas as pd\nimport random\n# Define the optimization space for pity probabilities\nparam_space = [\n    Real(0.05, 0.2, name=\"pity_2\"),   # Pity for 2nd draw\n    Real(0.1, 0.3, name=\"pity_3\"),    # Pity for 3rd draw\n    Real(0.15, 0.4, name=\"pity_4\"),   # Pity for 4th draw\n    Real(0.25, 0.55, name=\"pity_5\"),  # Pity for 5th draw\n    Real(0.5, 0.85, name=\"pity_6\")    # Pity for 6th draw\n]\n# Fixed values for 1st and 7th draws\nFIXED_PITY_VALUES = [0.0, 1.0]\n# Simulated bot play function\ndef simulate_pity_mechanic(pity_rates, num_simulations=500):\n    win_count = 0\n    for _ in range(num_simulations):\n        pulls = 0\n        while pulls < 7:\n            if random.random() < pity_rates[pulls]:\n                win_count += 1\n                break\n            pulls += 1\n    return win_count / num_simulations  # Return win rate percentage\n# Load base win rates per level (assumed calculated separately)\nbase_win_rates = {level: random.uniform(40, 60) for level in range(1, 16)}  # Simulated base win rates\n@use_named_args(param_space)\ndef objective(**params):\n    pity_rates = [FIXED_PITY_VALUES[0]] + [params[f\"pity_{i}\"] for i in range(2, 7)] + [FIXED_PITY_VALUES[1]]\n    total_loss = 0\n    for level in range(1, 16):\n        win_rate = simulate_pity_mechanic(pity_rates)\n        target_win_rate = base_win_rates[level]\n        total_loss += abs(win_rate * 100 - target_win_rate)\n    return total_loss / 15\nresult = gp_minimize(objective, param_space, n_calls=20, random_state=42)\nbest_pity_values = [FIXED_PITY_VALUES[0]] + result.x + [FIXED_PITY_VALUES[1]]\nimport ace_tools as tools\noptimized_results = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"Pull Number\": list(range(1, 8)),\n    \"Optimized Pity Probability\": best_pity_values\n})\ntools.display_dataframe_to_user(name=\"Optimized Pity Mechanic Parameters\", dataframe=optimized_results)\n```", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-03-15T18:19:38Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-09-16T02:22:21Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 482475, "labels": ["Levels", "Cappadocia", "Bot", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-03-06T04:17:20Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-15T18:19:38Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2144", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2216", "record": {"id": "ENG-2216", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_63fffeb4fab5233e", "creator_id": "usr_63fffeb4fab5233e", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2216", "number": 2216, "title": "Run Bayesian Optimization to Determine Adaptive Pity Parameters", "description": "Now that we have the **baseline pity parameters**, the next step is to **optimize adaptive pity mechanics** using **Bayesian Optimization**.\n\n---\n\n## **1. Objective: Fine-Tune Adaptive Pity Mechanics**\n\nAdaptive pity mechanics **adjust dynamically** based on:\n\n* **Hand tiles left**\n* **Board tiles left**\n* **Retry count average**\n\nWe aim to **find the best adaptive pity adjustments** that: \u2705 Ensure a **near-miss experience**\n\u2705 Keep the **win rate close to target**\n\u2705 Prevent **overcompensation**\n\n---\n\n## **2. Parameters to Optimize**\n\nWe will fine-tune the **adaptive pity rule adjustments**:\n\n| **Adaptive Pity Type** | **Current Adjustment** | **Optimization Range** |\n| -- | -- | -- |\n| **Hand Tiles Left (\u22643)** | `+0.3f` | `[0.2 - 0.5]` |\n| **Hand Tiles Left (3-6)** | `+0.2f` | `[0.1 - 0.3]` |\n| **Hand Tiles Left (6-10)** | `-1 (no effect)` | `[0.0 - 0.1]` |\n| **Board Tiles Left (\u22656)** | `+0.2f` | `[0.1 - 0.4]` |\n| **Board Tiles Left (3-5)** | `+0.1f` | `[0.05 - 0.2]` |\n| **Retry Count Average (\u22651.75)** | `+0.25f` | `[0.15 - 0.4]` |\n| **Retry Count Average (1.5-1.74)** | `+0.15f` | `[0.1 - 0.3]` |\n| **Retry Count Average (1.25-1.49)** | `+0.05f` | `[0.01 - 0.1]` |\n\n---\n\n## **3. Bayesian Optimization Approach**\n\nBayesian Optimization will:\n\n1. **Select an initial set of adaptive pity adjustments**.\n2. **Simulate win rates across levels**.\n3. **Use Gaussian Processes (GPs)** to predict the best parameters.\n4. **Refine the values iteratively**.\n\n### **Objective Function**\n\nLoss=\u2211level\u2223Simulated\u00a0Win\u00a0Rate\u2212Target\u00a0Win\u00a0Rate\u2223\\\\text{Loss} = \\\\sum\\_{level} | \\\\text{Simulated Win Rate} - \\\\text{Target Win Rate} |Loss=level\u2211\u2223Simulated\u00a0Win\u00a0Rate\u2212Target\u00a0Win\u00a0Rate\u2223\n\nLower values are better.\n\n---\n\n## **4. Implementing Bayesian Optimization in Python**\n\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport skopt\nfrom skopt import gp_minimize\nfrom skopt.space import Real\nfrom skopt.utils import use_named_args\nimport pandas as pd\nimport random\n\n# Define the optimization space for adaptive pity mechanics\nparam_space = [\n    Real(0.2, 0.5, name=\"hand_tiles_3\"),   # Hand tiles \u22643\n    Real(0.1, 0.3, name=\"hand_tiles_6\"),   # Hand tiles 3-6\n    Real(0.0, 0.1, name=\"hand_tiles_10\"),  # Hand tiles 6-10\n    Real(0.1, 0.4, name=\"board_tiles_6\"),  # Board tiles \u22656\n    Real(0.05, 0.2, name=\"board_tiles_3\"), # Board tiles 3-5\n    Real(0.15, 0.4, name=\"retry_1.75\"),    # Retry count \u22651.75\n    Real(0.1, 0.3, name=\"retry_1.5\"),      # Retry count 1.5-1.74\n    Real(0.01, 0.1, name=\"retry_1.25\")     # Retry count 1.25-1.49\n]\n\n# Load base win rates per level (from previous simulation)\nbase_win_rates = {level: random.uniform(40, 60) for level in range(1, 16)}  # Simulated base win rates\n\n# Simulated bot play function\ndef simulate_adaptive_pity(pity_adjustments, num_simulations=500):\n    win_count = 0\n    for _ in range(num_simulations):\n        hand_tiles = random.randint(0, 10)\n        board_tiles = random.randint(1, 20)\n        retries = random.uniform(1.0, 2.0)\n        \n        pity_bonus = 0.0\n        if hand_tiles <= 3:\n            pity_bonus += pity_adjustments[\"hand_tiles_3\"]\n        elif hand_tiles <= 6:\n            pity_bonus += pity_adjustments[\"hand_tiles_6\"]\n        elif hand_tiles <= 10:\n            pity_bonus += pity_adjustments[\"hand_tiles_10\"]\n\n        if board_tiles >= 6:\n            pity_bonus += pity_adjustments[\"board_tiles_6\"]\n        elif board_tiles >= 3:\n            pity_bonus += pity_adjustments[\"board_tiles_3\"]\n\n        if retries >= 1.75:\n            pity_bonus += pity_adjustments[\"retry_1.75\"]\n        elif retries >= 1.5:\n            pity_bonus += pity_adjustments[\"retry_1.5\"]\n        elif retries >= 1.25:\n            pity_bonus += pity_adjustments[\"retry_1.25\"]\n\n        win_probability = min(0.6 + pity_bonus, 1.0)  # Ensuring the cap\n        if random.random() < win_probability:\n            win_count += 1\n\n    return win_count / num_simulations  # Return win rate percentage\n\n@use_named_args(param_space)\ndef objective(**params):\n    total_loss = 0\n    for level in range(1, 16):  # Optimize for first 15 levels\n        win_rate = simulate_adaptive_pity(params)\n        target_win_rate = base_win_rates[level]\n        total_loss += abs(win_rate * 100 - target_win_rate)\n\n    return total_loss / 15  # Average loss across levels\n\n# Run Bayesian Optimization\nresult = gp_minimize(objective, param_space, n_calls=20, random_state=42)\n\n# Best found parameters\nbest_adaptive_pity_values = {param_space[i].name: result.x[i] for i in range(len(param_space))}\n\nimport ace_tools as tools\n# Store optimized adaptive pity mechanic settings\noptimized_adaptive_results = pd.DataFrame(best_adaptive_pity_values.items(), columns=[\"Adaptive Pity Parameter\", \"Optimized Value\"])\ntools.display_dataframe_to_user(name=\"Optimized Adaptive Pity Mechanic Parameters\", dataframe=optimized_adaptive_results)\n```", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-03-15T18:19:29Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-09-16T02:22:21Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 482475, "labels": ["Cappadocia", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-03-06T04:35:58Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-15T18:19:29Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2145", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2217", "record": {"id": "ENG-2217", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_63fffeb4fab5233e", "creator_id": "usr_63fffeb4fab5233e", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2217", "number": 2217, "title": "Optimize Pre-Level Parameters for Target Win Rates using Bayesian Optimization", "description": "**Objective:** To determine the optimal pre-level parameters that achieve specific target win rates of **90%, 75%, 60%, 45%, and 30%** with a **5% margin of error** using Bayesian Optimization.\n\n---\n\n**Scope:** This optimization process will fine-tune the following pre-level parameters:\n\n1. **Win Streak Adjustments** (Chops-based bonuses for consecutive wins):\n   * Win Streak 1 \u2192 +1 Chop\n   * Win Streak 2 \u2192 +2 Chops\n   * Win Streak 3 \u2192 +3 Chops\n2. **Pre-Level Booster Adjustments**:\n   * Extra Tile \u2192 +1 Chop\n   * Extra Wild Tile \u2192 +2 Chops\n3. **Player Bucketing Adjustments** (Hand tile reductions based on average attempts to win):\n   * Top Bucket (1.00 - 1.25 avg attempts) \u2192 3 hand tile reduction\n   * Second Bucket (1.25 - 1.50 avg attempts) \u2192 2 hand tile reduction\n   * Third Bucket (1.50 - 1.75 avg attempts) \u2192 1 hand tile reduction\n   * Bottom Bucket (1.75 - 10 avg attempts) \u2192 No hand tile reduction\n   * **Minimum hand tile count set to 5**\n4. **Character Level Scaling**:\n   * Level 0-20 \u2192 0 Chops\n   * Level 20-39 \u2192 +1 Chop\n   * Level 39+ \u2192 +2 Chops\n5. **Retry-Based Adjustments (Unique Symbol Count Reductions)**:\n   * If win rate over last **3 games is 0%** \u2192 Reduce unique symbol count by 1\n   * If win rate over last **6 games is 0%** \u2192 Reduce unique symbol count by 2\n\n---\n\n**Approach:**\n\n1. **Simulate bot plays for each pre-level configuration** using a Bayesian Optimization approach.\n2. **Compare win rates** against target win rates for **90%, 75%, 60%, 45%, and 30%**.\n3. **Adjust pre-level parameters iteratively** to minimize deviation from target win rates.\n4. **Optimize pre-level settings** by running multiple Bayesian Optimization iterations, fine-tuning variables to stabilize win rates within the acceptable range.\n\n---\n\n**Implementation Plan:**\n\n* **Step 1:** Run **baseline bot simulations** with existing pre-level parameters.\n* **Step 2:** Implement **Bayesian Optimization** to identify the best pre-level parameter values.\n* **Step 3:** Validate the optimized values across **multiple simulations** to ensure consistency.\n* **Step 4:** Finalize the pre-level parameter settings and deploy for live A/B testing.\n\n---\n\n**Expected Outcome:** \u2705 Identifies the best pre-level parameters to achieve **balanced difficulty across all target win rates**.\n\u2705 Uses **Bayesian Optimization** to efficiently fine-tune settings without brute-force testing.\n\u2705 Ensures a **smooth player experience** with **gradual difficulty adjustments based on performance**.\n\n---\n\n**Next Steps:**\n\n* Run the Bayesian Optimization script on **pre-level parameters**.\n* Evaluate the results and make adjustments as needed.\n* Conduct A/B tests to validate real player impact.", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-03-15T18:20:12Z", "completed_at": "2025-05-04T20:00:04Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-11-05T04:09:25Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 410374, "labels": ["Cappadocia", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-03-06T04:48:51Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-04T20:00:05Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2151", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2222", "record": {"id": "ENG-2222", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "creator_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2222", "number": 2222, "title": "River Rush: Update bots after finishing each stage", "description": null, "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-03-10T19:43:32Z", "completed_at": "2025-03-18T16:24:21Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-09-19T02:27:08Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 478270, "labels": ["Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-03-10T19:43:32Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-18T16:24:21Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2154", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2225", "record": {"id": "ENG-2225", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Canceled", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2225", "number": 2225, "title": "The weekly leaderboard bot scores are too squeezed in a small range.", "description": "[ScreenRecording_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6109]_1.MP4]([URL_52188])", "priority": 0, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": null, "canceled_at": "2025-03-26T16:44:37Z", "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 466730, "labels": ["Bug"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-03-13T13:53:52Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-26T16:44:37Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2156", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2227", "record": {"id": "ENG-2227", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_4e13bd40cc73d0fc", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2227", "number": 2227, "title": "Losing flow for river rush is not Implemented properly", "description": "Version or date: Dev_iOS_1276\n\n### Description: \n\n* There is no losing condition implemented. If a bot wins the event,\n  * I didn't see the race scene with another player wining the event. Instead, the event directly terminated and no status text on the event icon.\n  * I should see the race scene and continue button instead of \"Claim\" or \"Play\".\n    * When I click on the \"Continue\" button, I should see the losing screen. And losing screen should direct me to the join pop up again.\n  * The same stage race should restart with new bots and progression. It starts with new bots but player's progress are not updated.\n\n### Visual References:\n\n[Record_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6112]_64875109357c738d09c3691cefc5a1e4.mp4]([URL_52194])\n\n* Event loss screen\n\n  ![image.png]([URL_52193])\n* Lost event race scene \n\n  ![image.png]([URL_52192])\n\n![image.png]([URL_52191])\n\n### Expected Outcome: \n\n1. to show the river race screen with different player won. \n2. To show continue button\n3. Continue button will direct the join pop up\n4. join pop up will highlight the same race stage\n5. reset race progress and start it with the new bots with no progression", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-03-18T16:24:44Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 478270, "labels": ["Cappadocia", "Bug", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-2228", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-03-17T11:12:30Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-18T16:24:44Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2157", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2228", "record": {"id": "ENG-2228", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "creator_id": "usr_65c76e0b87aa7e9b", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2228", "number": 2228, "title": "Bots in river rush doesn't wait player's event initiation", "description": "Version or date: Dev_iOS_1276\n\n### Description: \n\n* The bots in river rush are progressing in river rush event when the event timer starts. However, event timer doesn't mean that the race is started for players.\n* Rather than event timer, it should start progressing after player starts the race session. \n  * But every singular race stage should be reset when they first started.  \n\n### Visual References:\n\n[ScreenRecording_[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6113]_1.MP4]([URL_52195])\n\n### Expected Outcome: is to start bot progress when any stage is started by player. \n\n* Always start with new bots when player click on the start button of the event.  \n\n### Steps to Repro:\n\n1. Unlock River Rush\n2. Start the race 10 minutes after event refreshes\n3. Observe that bots will already going forward when the event is started", "priority": 1, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-03-18T16:24:42Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 478270, "labels": ["Cappadocia", "Bug", "Sprint 30 Cappadocia -  Feb 28th"], "links": [], "relations": [{"target": "ENG-2227", "type": "relates"}], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-03-17T11:28:10Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-18T16:24:42Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2160", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2230", "record": {"id": "ENG-2230", "project_id": "1061a4f4-bc6a-45ca-a5b6-7f73d5e0abe2", "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_bdf01b53c6a92c5e", "creator_id": "usr_c77c50cc15c5342d", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2230", "number": 2230, "title": "Season Pass Vfx Animations Implementation", "description": "[Bonus bank filling animation001.mp4]([URL_52208])\n\n[check and claim 002.mp4]([URL_52207])\n\n[claimRewardSmall001.mp4]([URL_52206])\n\n[smallPadlockUnlock 001.mp4]([URL_52205])\n\n[Stage Unlock animation001.mp4]([URL_52204])\n\nFor the horisontal golden bars with the lock:\n\nTo unlock them the animation will start from the \"Fill ProgressBar Pivot\" game object:\n\n[[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6119].6756606.mp4]([URL_52203])\n\nSo the bar its jost a dotween animation that fills up and on complete activates a bunch of stuff, we have two options depending on what we are going to throw to the cell:\n\nWe have unlock the lockpad animation and we throw the particles to the golden chest in the bonus bank.\n\nDepending on what animation we want to achive we just set the correct game object active:\n\nfeedPower_Bank_Vfx it turns on the game object that goes to the powerbank\n\nUnlockProgress_Vfx it turns on the game object that goes to the lock pad.\n\nThe golden horisontal lines come in two versions\n\nUnlock version, wich is just unlock the pad and make the bars dissapear and\n\nLock version. wich makes the bars appear and the lock to appear.\n\n**For the unlock animation:**\n\n[[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6118].1425187.mp4]([URL_52202])\n\nwhen sparx_With_Trail particles inside of UnlockProgress_Vfx arive to the lockpad they will activate the Unlock game object u see there and inside the Unlock_UI_Element plays the unlocking animation and the bars to dissapear\n\nfor the bottom bar i had to add another season pass cell and in there is the bottom gold bar. (it to has two states . unlock and lock version)\n\nThe Lock version:\n\nThis animation we just want the bars to appear and the lockpad to appear\n\n[[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6117].4721244.mp4]([URL_52201])\n\nSo after we do the unlock version to make the bars dissapear and the pad, we need then to progress and make them reapear again. We just need to turn on the Lock_Version game object to play the animation.\n\n**Reward Unlock lockpad Animation:**\n\n[[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6116].6341140.mp4]([URL_52200])\n\n**For this animation we just need to turn on the Unlock game object wich it will turn off the icn - padlock - seasonpass game object (the icon of the closed padlock)**\n\nCheck and Claim animations:\n\n![image.png]([URL_52199])\n\n![image.png]([URL_52198])\n\nThey just got a dotween animation to make them appear .\n\n**Claim reward simbol animation:**\n\n[[CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER_6115].2147648.mp4]([URL_52197])\n\nWe have this little animation that makes the reward flying up. We should use this kind of animations for any other stuff thats similar in the future.\n\n---\n\nI just want to mention that the way i animate the progress bar at the top its not the correct way, i just using a dotween animation to scale it to fill it up, you probably going to need to animate it by code or something.\n\nFill ProgressBar Pivot\n\nI just used it to activate game objects and make particles play.\n\n---\n\nHey if you got any other questions please message me on slack!\n\nGood luck!", "priority": 2, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": null, "completed_at": "2025-05-05T09:38:58Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": null, "time_in_status_minutes": 409555, "labels": ["VFX Integration"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": false, "created_at": "2025-03-18T11:29:31Z", "updated_at": "2025-05-05T09:38:58Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2161", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2231", "record": {"id": "ENG-2231", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": null, "assignee_id": "usr_PERSON_3138", "creator_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2231", "number": 2231, "title": "Zombie game: Set up new server API", "description": null, "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-03-24T17:42:31Z", "completed_at": "2025-03-28T18:20:37Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-09-29T02:18:37Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 463754, "labels": ["Server/Cloud"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-03-24T17:42:31Z", "updated_at": "2025-03-28T18:20:37Z"}}, {"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/linear/data.json", "pointer": "/issues/2162", "field": "id", "value": "ENG-2232", "record": {"id": "ENG-2232", "project_id": null, "team_id": "team_ENG", "parent_id": "ENG-2231", "assignee_id": "usr_PERSON_3138", "creator_id": "usr_cd7849ec043ab3da", "state_id": "Done", "cycle_id": null, "identifier": "ENG-2232", "number": 2232, "title": "Set up SSL certificate", "description": null, "priority": 3, "estimate": null, "due_date": null, "started_at": "2025-03-25T00:07:28Z", "completed_at": "2025-03-25T16:57:47Z", "canceled_at": null, "archived_at": "2025-09-29T02:18:36Z", "time_in_status_minutes": 468156, "labels": ["Server/Cloud"], "links": [], "relations": [], "is_archived": true, "created_at": "2025-03-24T17:43:45Z", 